53
00:02:23,615 --> 00:02:25,350
♪ WANNA BE ON TOP ♪♪

54
00:02:40,460 --> 00:02:43,296
Tyra: FOR THE FIRST THREE CYCLES
OF "AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL",

55
00:02:43,296 --> 00:02:44,998
I TOOK THE GIRLS
TO NEW YORK CITY

56
00:02:44,998 --> 00:02:46,699
TO LEARN ABOUT
THE FASHION WORLD.

57
00:02:47,266 --> 00:02:49,268
♪♪♪

58
00:02:52,238 --> 00:02:54,340
THIS TIME, WE SHOOK THINGS UP.

59
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:57,210
YOU GUYS
ARE LIVING IN LOS ANGELES.

60
00:02:57,210 --> 00:02:59,278
(cheering)

61
00:02:59,545 --> 00:03:01,214
Tyra: I BROUGHT THIS GROUP
OF GIRLS TO THE CITY

62
00:03:01,214 --> 00:03:03,449
WHERE I GOT MY START,
LOS ANGELES.

63
00:03:03,449 --> 00:03:05,018
GREAT, I LOVE L.A.
SO LET'S STAY HERE.

64
00:03:05,018 --> 00:03:07,987
I AM FROM HERE
SO I AM VERY UNHAPPY

65
00:03:07,987 --> 00:03:10,690
THAT THE COMPETITION
IS NOW IN L.A.

66
00:03:11,324 --> 00:03:14,327
TODAY, THIS IS
YOUR FIRST PHOTO SHOOT.

67
00:03:14,327 --> 00:03:15,461
(cheering)

68
00:03:15,461 --> 00:03:16,596
TO KEEP THE GIRLS IN LINE,

69
00:03:16,596 --> 00:03:18,598
I SENT MY OWN
FASHION POLICE SQUAD.

70
00:03:18,598 --> 00:03:20,633
TOP MODEL JUDGES, NIGEL BARKER,

71
00:03:20,633 --> 00:03:23,102
NOLÉ MARIN,
AND MISS JANICE DICKINSON.

72
00:03:23,102 --> 00:03:25,538
BE AFRAID, BE VERY AFRAID.

73
00:03:25,538 --> 00:03:28,675
Kahlen: I THINK JANICE IS
EXTREMELY SCARY.

74
00:03:28,675 --> 00:03:31,177
SHE INTIMIDATES
THE CRAP OUT OF ME.

75
00:03:31,177 --> 00:03:33,346
WHERE DID THIS COME FROM?

76
00:03:33,346 --> 00:03:34,714
- Brandy: UM...
- Janice: THIS.

77
00:03:34,714 --> 00:03:36,049
THE BEAUTY SUPPLY STORE.

78
00:03:36,049 --> 00:03:37,083
Janice: WHAT ABOUT YOU?

79
00:03:37,083 --> 00:03:38,785
WHERE'D YOU GET THAT,
WHAT'S THIS?

80
00:03:38,785 --> 00:03:41,754
NO MORE TATTOOS.

81
00:03:41,754 --> 00:03:44,524
Brandy: WHY ARE YOU SO HARD
SOMETIMES?

82
00:03:44,524 --> 00:03:46,959
IF I'M NOT HARD ON YOU
IN THE BEGINNING,

83
00:03:46,959 --> 00:03:49,429
AND IF I DON'T SAY, YOU KNOW,
I GOT NEWS FOR YOU, BRANDY.

84
00:03:49,429 --> 00:03:52,532
IT AIN'T GONNA FLY
ON YOUR HAIR RIGHT NOW, BITCH,

85
00:03:52,532 --> 00:03:54,534
BECAUSE THE MINUTE YOU GET TO
"VOGUE" MAGAZINE,

86
00:03:54,534 --> 00:03:55,535
THEY'RE GONNA SAY "WHAT!"

87
00:03:55,535 --> 00:03:57,670
SO I'M ACTUALLY
DOING YOU A FAVOR.

88
00:03:57,670 --> 00:04:00,940
I'M JUST BITCH JUDGE,
GET USED TO IT.

89
00:04:02,742 --> 00:04:04,911
Tyra: THERE WERE A LOT OF THINGS
THE GIRLS HAD TO GET USED TO.

90
00:04:04,911 --> 00:04:07,180
OOH, OH, THERE.

91
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:09,415
Tyra: LIKE SLIPPERY PROPS.

92
00:04:10,650 --> 00:04:12,285
UNCOMFORTABLE CLOTHING.

93
00:04:12,285 --> 00:04:15,221
MY FEET HURT REALLY BAD.

94
00:04:15,221 --> 00:04:17,123
THEY LIKE MADE ME SHOVE MY FEET
INTO THESE THINGS

95
00:04:17,123 --> 00:04:18,991
AND I CAN'T EVEN WALK IN 'EM.

96
00:04:18,991 --> 00:04:21,761
I'M SORRY, I'VE SHOVED MY FEET
INTO THINGS BEFORE

97
00:04:21,761 --> 00:04:24,097
- BUT THIS REALLY HURTS.
- ALL RIGHT.

98
00:04:24,097 --> 00:04:26,299
SHE'S A MODEL, SHE NEEDS TO
LEARN HOW TO WORK IT.

99
00:04:26,299 --> 00:04:30,436
Tyra: AND LONG,
LONG, LONG HOURS.

100
00:04:30,436 --> 00:04:32,772
BRANDY NOT FEELING IT RIGHT NOW.

101
00:04:32,772 --> 00:04:34,173
WHY NOT?

102
00:04:34,173 --> 00:04:36,576
Brandy: 'CAUSE I WAS WAITING
SO LONG, I'M NOT GONNA LIE.

103
00:04:36,576 --> 00:04:38,678
Nigel: BRANDY, BRANDY, BRANDY,
YOU CAN BE AS MISERABLE

104
00:04:38,678 --> 00:04:39,946
AS YOU LIKE
IN BETWEEN SHOTS,

105
00:04:39,946 --> 00:04:41,247
WHEN YOU COME ONTO THE SET,

106
00:04:41,247 --> 00:04:44,851
I'M LOOKING FOR SOMEONE THAT'S
GONNA WOW EVERYBODY.

107
00:04:44,851 --> 00:04:47,220
Tyra: BRITA HAD BEEN WAITING
EVEN LONGER

108
00:04:47,220 --> 00:04:48,721
TO START A MODELING CAREER.

109
00:04:48,721 --> 00:04:51,457
I'M 25, I'M NOT 18, I KNOW
I ONLY HAVE A COUPLE MORE YEARS

110
00:04:51,457 --> 00:04:53,359
BEFORE PEOPLE ARE GONNA START
THINKING I'M TOO OLD.

111
00:04:53,359 --> 00:04:55,094
IT'S KIND OF A MAKE IT
OR BREAK IT POINT.

112
00:04:55,094 --> 00:04:56,662
Tyra: BUT ON SET,
HER SELF-CONSCIOUSNESS

113
00:04:56,662 --> 00:04:58,097
GOT THE BEST OF HER.

114
00:04:58,097 --> 00:05:01,100
Brita: I'M WEARING COMPLETELY
SHEER UNDERWEAR, AND I'M SORRY--

115
00:05:01,100 --> 00:05:02,602
I CAN'T POSITION TO BE
COMFORTABLE

116
00:05:02,602 --> 00:05:05,037
WHEN MY SKIRT KEEPS FALLING UP.

117
00:05:05,037 --> 00:05:06,205
SHE'S GOT A SIDE OF BEEF.

118
00:05:08,174 --> 00:05:10,176
Tyra: THE GIRLS WERE DEAD TIRED
AFTER THE SHOOT,

119
00:05:10,176 --> 00:05:12,612
BUT THEY CAME BACK TO LIFE
WHEN THEY SAW THEIR NEW HOME,

120
00:05:12,612 --> 00:05:15,414
A LUXURIOUS LOFT
IN DOWNTOWN L.A.

121
00:05:15,414 --> 00:05:18,384
YES, YES, YES...

122
00:05:18,384 --> 00:05:22,021
OH MY GOD!

123
00:05:22,021 --> 00:05:23,256
OH MY GOD!

124
00:05:23,256 --> 00:05:24,757
Sarah:
OUR NEW HOME IS INCREDIBLE,

125
00:05:24,757 --> 00:05:26,058
IT'S MORE THAN WE THOUGHT.

126
00:05:26,058 --> 00:05:29,395
THE NEW HOUSE IS BEAUTIFUL.

127
00:05:29,395 --> 00:05:31,497
OH MY GOD.

128
00:05:32,298 --> 00:05:34,700
Tyra: AS THE OTHER GIRLS STARTED
TO SETTLE IN...

129
00:05:34,700 --> 00:05:36,969
WE'RE LIVING IN
MODELWOOD, BABY.

130
00:05:36,969 --> 00:05:38,905
Tyra: BRANDY STARTED TO
COMPLAIN.

131
00:05:38,905 --> 00:05:40,339
SORRY, Y'ALL HAVE PLANS?

132
00:05:40,339 --> 00:05:41,507
I DON'T HAVE TIME.

133
00:05:41,507 --> 00:05:43,376
I DON'T NEED ALL THESE
LIGHT FOODS, OKAY.

134
00:05:43,376 --> 00:05:47,046
I EAT FAT, I EAT FAT,
I EAT FOOD WITH FAT, OKAY?

135
00:05:47,046 --> 00:05:50,016
Tatiana: BRANDY, I'VE NOTICED
THAT SHE'S GRUMPY AT TIMES,

136
00:05:50,016 --> 00:05:51,684
HAS A BAD ATTITUDE

137
00:05:51,684 --> 00:05:53,152
AND IF YOU PUT
NEGATIVE ENERGY OUT,

138
00:05:53,152 --> 00:05:54,353
IT'S GONNA COME BACK TO YOU.

139
00:05:54,353 --> 00:05:55,721
WHERE'S OUR SUITCASES?

140
00:05:55,721 --> 00:05:58,324
RIGHT THERE!
GIRL, Y'ALL GOING CRAZY.

141
00:05:58,324 --> 00:06:00,960
Tyra: THE NEXT DAY, BRANDY
WOKE UP WITH A FEW KINKS

142
00:06:00,960 --> 00:06:02,261
THAT SHE NEEDED TO WORK OUT.

143
00:06:02,261 --> 00:06:04,797
OH MY GOD, THIS IS A KNOT.

144
00:06:04,797 --> 00:06:07,500
YESTERDAY, THE MAN MESSED UP
MY HAIR, TEASING IT...

145
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:09,535
I'M LOOKING LIKE A FOOL.

146
00:06:09,535 --> 00:06:11,604
NO, YOU LOOK BEAUTIFUL.

147
00:06:12,738 --> 00:06:13,940
I MEAN, COME ON.

148
00:06:13,940 --> 00:06:16,609
OKAY, TOLD HER, JUST--
JUST TELL THE TRUTH.

149
00:06:16,609 --> 00:06:18,811
THEY'RE GONNA GIVE ME
A MAKEOVER ANYWAYS.

150
00:06:20,012 --> 00:06:22,648
BUT BRANDY WASN'T THE ONLY ONE
HAVING A BAD HAIR DAY.

151
00:06:22,648 --> 00:06:25,284
IT WAS TIME
FOR THE GIRLS TO BE MADE OVER.

152
00:06:25,284 --> 00:06:26,552
SARAH, WE'RE GONNA GIVE YOU

153
00:06:26,552 --> 00:06:29,755
A VERY PETER PAN
INSPIRED HAIRCUT.

154
00:06:29,755 --> 00:06:32,925
MICHELLE, WE'RE GONNA MAKE YOU
ICE BLONDE GIRL.

155
00:06:32,925 --> 00:06:35,461
MY BRANDY,
WE HAVE THOUGHT ABOUT YOU

156
00:06:35,461 --> 00:06:36,929
AND WE'VE DECIDED, GIRL,

157
00:06:36,929 --> 00:06:40,700
THAT YOU ARE... FIERCE!

158
00:06:40,700 --> 00:06:43,536
AND WE AIN'T DOING
NOTHING TO YOU!

159
00:06:43,536 --> 00:06:45,371
NADA.

160
00:06:45,371 --> 00:06:46,806
Brandy: WHEN SHE TOLD ME
I WAS GONNA KEEP THE AFRO,

161
00:06:46,806 --> 00:06:48,040
I WAS JUST LIKE,

162
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:51,344
WHY, BECAUSE I WANTED
A DRASTIC CHANGE SO BAD.

163
00:06:51,344 --> 00:06:53,446
Tyra: BUT AFTER I TOOK A CLOSER
LOOK AT BRANDY'S HAIR,

164
00:06:53,446 --> 00:06:55,748
I DECIDED SHE DID
NEED A MAKEOVER.

165
00:06:55,748 --> 00:06:58,217
BRANDY, I'M GONNA HAVE
TO TAKE THIS OFF, PRECIOUS.

166
00:06:58,217 --> 00:06:59,552
IT'S LIKE MATTED.

167
00:06:59,552 --> 00:07:01,287
♪♪♪

168
00:07:05,758 --> 00:07:08,027
JUST DO ME GOOD,
JUST DO ME GOOD.

169
00:07:08,027 --> 00:07:10,396
Tyra: SOME GIRLS WERE EXCITED
ABOUT THEIR MAKEOVERS.

170
00:07:10,396 --> 00:07:12,064
I'M READY TO LOOK HOT.

171
00:07:12,064 --> 00:07:13,566
Tyra: SOME GIRLS WERE WORRIED.

172
00:07:13,566 --> 00:07:15,034
YOU GUYS DO THIS ALL THE TIME?

173
00:07:16,736 --> 00:07:18,404
WHEN THEY TOLD ME THEY WERE
GONNA CUT OFF MY HAIR,

174
00:07:18,404 --> 00:07:19,805
I WAS A LITTLE NERVOUS.

175
00:07:19,805 --> 00:07:21,140
YOU'RE OUTTA CONTROL
WITH THE SCISSORS.

176
00:07:21,140 --> 00:07:22,575
Tyra: BUT WHEN THEY SAW
THE FINAL RESULTS,

177
00:07:22,575 --> 00:07:24,143
THEY ALL FELT FABULOUS.

178
00:07:24,143 --> 00:07:25,945
- THAT LOOKS GREAT.
- INCREDIBLE.

179
00:07:25,945 --> 00:07:28,147
I LOVE IT,
I LOVE IT-I LOVE IT-I LOVE IT.

180
00:07:28,147 --> 00:07:29,515
EXCEPT BRANDY.

181
00:07:29,515 --> 00:07:31,951
WHOA.

182
00:07:31,951 --> 00:07:33,319
WHERE ARE THE EYEBROWS?

183
00:07:33,319 --> 00:07:36,756
YOU KNOW, I CAN'T EVEN BE SEXY--
OH MY GOD.

184
00:07:37,223 --> 00:07:39,525
Tyra: WHEN I CAME BACK IN
TO CHECK IN ON THE GIRLS,

185
00:07:39,525 --> 00:07:41,427
I HEARD THERE'D BEEN
SOME ATTITUDE.

186
00:07:41,427 --> 00:07:43,162
YOU PISSED ME OFF.

187
00:07:43,162 --> 00:07:46,599
I DON'T APPRECIATE THAT,
AND YOU KNOW WHO YOU ARE.

188
00:07:46,599 --> 00:07:48,801
THE NEXT TIME I SEE YOU
WILL BE AT JUDGING.

189
00:07:48,801 --> 00:07:50,303
♪♪♪

190
00:07:51,537 --> 00:07:54,674
AT JUDGING, IT CAME DOWN
TO BRANDY'S BAD ATTITUDE

191
00:07:54,674 --> 00:07:56,275
AND BRITA'S BAD PHOTO.

192
00:07:56,275 --> 00:07:58,744
YOU'RE FINE AS HECK IN PERSON,
BUT ON FILM,

193
00:07:58,744 --> 00:08:00,246
IT'S JUST NOT WORKING.

194
00:08:00,246 --> 00:08:02,581
YOU LOOK WORRIED,
YOU LOOK OLD.

195
00:08:02,581 --> 00:08:04,951
Tyra:
BRANDY, WHY DO YOU ACT THIS WAY?

196
00:08:04,951 --> 00:08:08,521
TO TRY TO BE...
I GUESS, REAL.

197
00:08:08,521 --> 00:08:11,590
THERE'S A DIFFERENCE BETWEEN
BEING REAL AND PROFESSIONAL.

198
00:08:11,590 --> 00:08:12,892
THERE'S SOMEWHERE IN THE MIDDLE.

199
00:08:12,892 --> 00:08:15,227
IF YOU GO ON A JOB INTERVIEW,
YOU KEEP IT REAL?

200
00:08:15,227 --> 00:08:17,930
AND SAY, "I'M TIRED, I BEEN UP
ALL NIGHT, MY BABY WAS CRYING.

201
00:08:17,930 --> 00:08:19,799
AND WHAT YOU NEED ME TO DO?"
SURE, THAT'S REAL.

202
00:08:19,799 --> 00:08:21,767
DOES ANYBODY WANNA HIRE YOU?

203
00:08:21,767 --> 00:08:23,502
REAL IS HOLDING ONTO YOUR SPIRIT

204
00:08:23,502 --> 00:08:26,272
BUT ADAPTING TO YOUR
SURROUNDINGS.

205
00:08:26,272 --> 00:08:27,840
YOUR ATTITUDE ISN'T SOMETHING

206
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:29,742
THAT THESE JUDGES
WANNA BE AROUND.

207
00:08:29,742 --> 00:08:31,577
BUT SOME OF THEM DO.

208
00:08:31,577 --> 00:08:34,113
THE JUDGES STILL SAW POTENTIAL
IN BRANDY,

209
00:08:34,113 --> 00:08:36,115
SO THEY DECIDED
TO SENT BRITA HOME.

210
00:08:39,085 --> 00:08:41,153
THE NEXT MORNING,
THE GIRLS TOOK THEIR FIRST STEPS

211
00:08:41,153 --> 00:08:43,055
TOWARD BECOMING TRUE TOP MODELS.

212
00:08:43,055 --> 00:08:47,793
A RUNWAY LESSON FROM THE CATWALK
DIVA HIMSELF, MISS J. ALEXANDER.

213
00:08:47,793 --> 00:08:49,361
(cheering)

214
00:08:49,361 --> 00:08:55,201
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL, YAY!

215
00:08:55,201 --> 00:08:57,269
Tyra: WHO CHEERED THEM
ON THROUGH A CRASH WALK

216
00:08:57,269 --> 00:08:58,337
IN WALKING THE WALK.

217
00:08:58,337 --> 00:08:59,939
BAM, HIT IT.

218
00:08:59,939 --> 00:09:02,608
IT'S NOT EASY WALKING ON GRASS,
IS IT?

219
00:09:02,608 --> 00:09:05,144
REBECCA ATTACKED
THE LESSON WITH CONFIDENCE.

220
00:09:05,144 --> 00:09:07,580
I'VE BEEN IN JUST A FEW LOCAL
MALL RUNWAY SHOWS.

221
00:09:07,580 --> 00:09:09,215
SO I JUST DO WHAT
FEELS NATURAL TO ME,

222
00:09:09,215 --> 00:09:10,950
SO I AM FAIRLY COMFORTABLE
WITH MY BODY,

223
00:09:10,950 --> 00:09:12,752
IN THE WAY IT MOVES
AND THE WAY I WANT IT TO MOVE.

224
00:09:12,752 --> 00:09:15,087
Tyra: BUT OTHER GIRLS WERE
HAVING PROBLEMS.

225
00:09:15,087 --> 00:09:16,689
MICHELLE,
YOU WALK LIKE YOU HAVE A BIT

226
00:09:16,689 --> 00:09:18,557
OF BELL'S PALSEY
ON THE RIGHT SIDE

227
00:09:18,557 --> 00:09:19,859
BECAUSE YOU WALK LIKE THIS.

228
00:09:19,859 --> 00:09:21,894
♪♪♪

229
00:09:21,894 --> 00:09:25,064
SARAH, PICK IT UP, PICK IT UP.

230
00:09:25,064 --> 00:09:26,932
Sarah: GROWING UP,
I WAS THE TOMBOY.

231
00:09:26,932 --> 00:09:30,536
I WAS VERY SKINNY AND STRAIGHT
UNTIL I WAS LIKE 16 YEARS OLD,

232
00:09:30,536 --> 00:09:33,939
AND I JUST WORKED MY BUTT OFF
TO BE WHERE I AM RIGHT NOW.

233
00:09:33,939 --> 00:09:36,742
I FEEL LIKE I'M AT THE RACES
AT THE TORTOISE AND THE HARE,

234
00:09:36,742 --> 00:09:39,345
AND SARAH, YOU'RE THE TORTOISE.

235
00:09:39,345 --> 00:09:42,548
Tyra: STILL SARAH FELT SHE WAS
FAR FROM THE WORST WALKER.

236
00:09:42,548 --> 00:09:44,083
LET ME JUST SHOW YOU WHAT
I WAS JUST TELLING CHRISTINA.

237
00:09:44,083 --> 00:09:45,518
- YEAH, I WANNA SEE.
- OKAY.

238
00:09:45,518 --> 00:09:46,886
I LOVE IMPRESSIONS.

239
00:09:46,886 --> 00:09:48,287
THIS IS HOW I WALK.

240
00:09:48,287 --> 00:09:50,022
OKAY, GRANTED, IT'S NOT
THAT GREAT, BUT WHATEVER, OKAY.

241
00:09:50,022 --> 00:09:51,023
SO I'M GONNA SHOW HERS.

242
00:09:54,093 --> 00:09:56,028
I DON'T WALK LIKE THAT!

243
00:09:56,028 --> 00:09:58,030
I'M JUST NOT THAT BAD,
I'M NOT THAT BAD.

244
00:10:00,933 --> 00:10:02,768
Tyra: SARAH'S TROUBLES CONTINUED
TO DOG HER

245
00:10:02,768 --> 00:10:04,036
IN THE NEXT PHOTO SHOOT.

246
00:10:04,036 --> 00:10:05,337
Woman: I DON'T FEEL LIKE
YOU'RE CONNECTING WITH ME.

247
00:10:05,337 --> 00:10:07,239
I THINK YOU'RE LOOKING TOO MUCH
AT THE SET.

248
00:10:07,239 --> 00:10:08,274
CHIN UP, CHIN UP!

249
00:10:08,274 --> 00:10:10,076
I NEED YOU TO CONNECT
WITH ME FASTER.

250
00:10:10,076 --> 00:10:11,877
WHEN IT COMES DOWN TO IT,
I DON'T KNOW IF I HAVE AS MUCH

251
00:10:11,877 --> 00:10:15,014
POTENTIAL AS THE NEXT PERSON HAS
SO IT'S A LITTLE NERVE-WRACKING.

252
00:10:15,014 --> 00:10:17,850
Tyra: ALTHOUGH, SARAH FELL FLAT,
REBECCA WAS UNSHAKEABLE.

253
00:10:17,850 --> 00:10:21,220
Woman: I LOVE IT,
THERE YOU GO, YEAH!

254
00:10:22,488 --> 00:10:24,890
Tyra: UNTIL A SHOCKING SURPRISE
AT JUDGING.

255
00:10:24,890 --> 00:10:26,592
YOU NEED TO WORK ON
YOUR PRESENCE.

256
00:10:26,592 --> 00:10:29,628
I DIDN'T FEEL THAT YOU EMBRACE--

257
00:10:29,628 --> 00:10:31,063
OH MY GOD.

258
00:10:31,063 --> 00:10:32,298
(gasping)

259
00:10:32,298 --> 00:10:34,333
OH MY GOD, SOMEBODY CALL
THE AMBULANCE.

260
00:10:34,333 --> 00:10:36,302
I'M CALLING 9-1-1,
I GOT IT.

261
00:10:36,302 --> 00:10:40,439
♪♪♪

262
00:10:40,439 --> 00:10:41,807
YOU LOOK REALLY PRETTY.

263
00:10:41,807 --> 00:10:44,410
THE MOST IMPORTANT THING,
YOU LOOK LIKE A SUPER MODEL.

264
00:10:44,710 --> 00:10:48,514
(siren blaring)

265
00:10:48,514 --> 00:10:49,815
YOU KNOW, I'M SURE THE GIRLS...

266
00:10:49,815 --> 00:10:52,118
I JUST GOT NERVOUS
AND I HAD AN ANXIETY ATTACK.

267
00:10:52,118 --> 00:10:54,587
FOR 19 YEARS, I'VE HAD
A CONDITION WHERE, YOU KNOW,

268
00:10:54,587 --> 00:10:56,889
I PASS OUT FOR NO REASON,
ANYWHERE, ANYTIME.

269
00:10:56,889 --> 00:10:57,923
DOESN'T MATTER.

270
00:10:57,923 --> 00:11:00,793
BUT IF I'M NOT ELIMINATED
TONIGHT,

271
00:11:00,793 --> 00:11:03,729
I WILL BE BACK TOMORROW,
STRONGER THAN EVER.

272
00:11:03,729 --> 00:11:05,831
I'M NOT GONNA
LET THIS GET ME DOWN.

273
00:11:05,831 --> 00:11:09,869
(sobbing)

274
00:11:09,869 --> 00:11:12,771
Tyra: FEELING BETTER THAT NIGHT,
REBECCA WAS ABLE TO RETURN.

275
00:11:12,771 --> 00:11:16,208
REBECCA.

276
00:11:16,208 --> 00:11:19,612
YOU SCARED ALL OF US
SO MUCH TONIGHT, REBECCA.

277
00:11:19,612 --> 00:11:21,046
I KNOW, I'M SO SORRY.

278
00:11:21,046 --> 00:11:24,450
BUT I ADMIRE YOUR TENACITY
AND I ADMIRE YOU RETURNING.

279
00:11:24,450 --> 00:11:27,052
THOUGH REBECCA RECOVERED
FROM HER FAINTING SPELL,

280
00:11:27,052 --> 00:11:29,121
IN THE END,
SARAH COULDN'T RECOVER

281
00:11:29,121 --> 00:11:31,857
FROM HER SHAKY WALK
AND STIFF PHOTO

282
00:11:34,460 --> 00:11:36,061
SO MUCH HAS HAPPENED THIS CYCLE

283
00:11:36,061 --> 00:11:38,364
THAT WE COULDN'T FIT
EVERYTHING IN.

284
00:11:38,364 --> 00:11:40,432
HERE'S ANOTHER MOMENT
FROM "TOP MODEL" VAULT

285
00:11:40,432 --> 00:11:41,700
YOU'VE NEVER SEEN BEFORE.

286
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:43,702
WHOO!
I LOVE LADY KAT.

287
00:11:43,702 --> 00:11:45,538
(meows)

288
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:49,708
(laughing)

289
00:11:49,708 --> 00:11:51,810
all: ONE, TWO, THREE, REOW!

290
00:11:51,810 --> 00:11:55,047
COMING UP, THE GIRLS BLOW OFF
SOME STEAM.

291
00:11:55,047 --> 00:11:57,716
- RUN!
- GET HER!

292
00:11:57,716 --> 00:12:00,920
AND BRITTANY GOES OVERBOARD.

293
00:12:03,189 --> 00:12:05,724
♪♪♪

294
00:12:07,126 --> 00:12:09,395
Tyra: SOMETIMES WHEN GIRLS COME
TO "AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL"

295
00:12:09,395 --> 00:12:12,364
THEY BRING BAGGAGE,
AND TIFFANY'S WAS HER TEMPER.

296
00:12:12,364 --> 00:12:15,901
(screaming)

297
00:12:15,901 --> 00:12:19,038
THAT STANK HO,
POURED THE BEER ON MY WEAVE.

298
00:12:19,038 --> 00:12:21,140
Tyra: BUT AFTER TAKING
ANGER MANAGEMENT CLASSES,

299
00:12:21,140 --> 00:12:22,942
SHE RETURNED
WITH A NEW ATTITUDE.

300
00:12:22,942 --> 00:12:24,710
I DON'T JUMP ON PEOPLE
AND THROW GLASSES

301
00:12:24,710 --> 00:12:26,278
AND STUFF LIKE THAT ANYMORE.

302
00:12:26,278 --> 00:12:27,513
Tyra:
HAVING CHANGED HER ATTITUDE,

303
00:12:27,513 --> 00:12:30,082
TIFFANY'S NEXT PROJECT
WAS BRANDY.

304
00:12:30,082 --> 00:12:31,483
I CALLED WAY IN THE KITCHEN.

305
00:12:31,483 --> 00:12:34,119
I SAID, AFTER NOELLE,
I WAS GONNA USE THE PHONE.

306
00:12:34,119 --> 00:12:36,855
YOU WEREN'T OUT HERE, SWEETIE,
WE'VE ALL BEEN WAITING IN LINE.

307
00:12:36,855 --> 00:12:39,558
I MEAN, IF Y'ALL WANNA GET RUDE
ABOUT IT, THEN WE CAN GET RUDE.

308
00:12:39,558 --> 00:12:41,060
WE WERE LIKE, WHAT IS THIS?

309
00:12:41,060 --> 00:12:44,897
YOU DO COME OFF LIKE A BITCH
SOMETIMES, YOU DO.

310
00:12:44,897 --> 00:12:46,131
AND YOU GOTTA CHANGE THAT.

311
00:12:46,131 --> 00:12:48,667
SO YOU GOTTA FIGURE OUT,
DO YOU WANNA BE A MODEL?

312
00:12:48,667 --> 00:12:50,236
OKAY, SO YOU NEED
TO CHANGE YOUR ATTITUDE

313
00:12:50,236 --> 00:12:52,004
'CAUSE YOUR ATTITUDE STINKS.

314
00:12:53,672 --> 00:12:54,640
Tyra:
BUT SOMETIMES

315
00:12:54,640 --> 00:12:56,742
THE OLD TIFFANY
WOULD TAKE CONTROL,

316
00:12:56,742 --> 00:12:58,143
AND SHE'D LOSE IT.

317
00:12:58,143 --> 00:13:00,713
THIS IS IT.

318
00:13:00,713 --> 00:13:03,482
Tatiana: I WOULD GO OVER THERE
AND HELP HER BUT, LIKE,

319
00:13:03,482 --> 00:13:05,618
THE SMELL OF VOMIT WILL MAKE ME
VOMIT MYSELF SO I'M LIKE,

320
00:13:05,618 --> 00:13:08,654
OKAY, I DON'T WANNA BE THE OTHER
GIRL THAT VOMITS, RIGHT?

321
00:13:08,654 --> 00:13:10,322
DON'T STEP IN IT,
DON'T STEP IN IT,

322
00:13:10,322 --> 00:13:12,024
DON'T STEP IN IT.

323
00:13:12,024 --> 00:13:14,193
Tyra: TIFFANY WAS STILL
PAYING FOR THAT DINNER

324
00:13:14,193 --> 00:13:15,594
THE NEXT MORNING.

325
00:13:15,594 --> 00:13:17,763
I THINK I'M STILL DRUNK.

326
00:13:17,763 --> 00:13:18,864
DRINK IT.

327
00:13:18,864 --> 00:13:20,466
I'M NOT DRINKING THAT,
THAT'S HORRIBLE.

328
00:13:20,466 --> 00:13:21,600
SISTER, YOU GOTTA DRINK IT.

329
00:13:23,836 --> 00:13:26,538
Tyra: BUT TIFFANY'S DAY WAS
ABOUT TO GET EVEN TOUGHER.

330
00:13:26,538 --> 00:13:28,540
ONE OF THE CHALLENGES
IN MODELING

331
00:13:28,540 --> 00:13:30,943
IS DEALING WITH
DIFFICULT PERSONALITIES.

332
00:13:30,943 --> 00:13:33,646
SO I ARRANGED FOR THE MODELS
TO MEET A TOUGH PHOTOGRAPHER.

333
00:13:33,646 --> 00:13:36,382
I WAS INSTRUCTED TO PRETTY MUCH
TEAR THEM TO SHREDS.

334
00:13:36,382 --> 00:13:38,250
LET'S DO IT!
OH!

335
00:13:38,250 --> 00:13:40,352
I COULD BRING A MULE OVER HERE
AND IT'LL GIVE ME

336
00:13:40,352 --> 00:13:42,321
A BETTER POSTURE AND BETTER
HITTING THE BALL, OKAY?

337
00:13:42,321 --> 00:13:44,556
HIT THE MARK,
THE MARK IS THERE FOR A REASON.

338
00:13:44,556 --> 00:13:46,158
AHH!

339
00:13:46,158 --> 00:13:48,327
WITHOUT THE FAKE SMILE,
LOSE THE FAKE SMILE!

340
00:13:48,327 --> 00:13:50,362
STOP, STOP WITH THE BALL,
STOP WITH THE BALL!

341
00:13:50,362 --> 00:13:52,564
- HERE GOES NOTHING.
- Alex: I HOPE NOT.

342
00:13:52,564 --> 00:13:54,667
Noelle:
I DON'T KNOW IF HE DIDN'T GET
HUGGED ENOUGH AS A CHILD,

343
00:13:54,667 --> 00:13:57,136
I JUST KNOW THAT HE'S MEAN,
AND I DON'T LIKE HIM.

344
00:13:57,136 --> 00:13:59,805
Alex: YOU CAN DO IT,
IT'S SIMPLE, IT IS.

345
00:13:59,805 --> 00:14:02,207
I'M REALLY LIKE GOING TO
HAPPY PLACE,

346
00:14:02,207 --> 00:14:03,342
HE'S FREAKING ME OUT.

347
00:14:03,342 --> 00:14:06,178
NO.

348
00:14:06,178 --> 00:14:09,048
Tyra: EVERY GIRL HANDLED
THE PRESSURE DIFFERENTLY.

349
00:14:09,048 --> 00:14:10,983
TIFFANY BARELY KEPT HERSELF
IN CHECK.

350
00:14:10,983 --> 00:14:13,519
Alex: WASTING MY TIME
AND EVERYBODY ELSE'S THEN.

351
00:14:13,519 --> 00:14:15,120
Tiffany:
I WANT TO POUND HIS HEAD IN

352
00:14:15,120 --> 00:14:16,655
WITH THAT TENNIS RACKET.

353
00:14:16,655 --> 00:14:18,324
Alex: DON'T LOOK SCARED,
YOU'RE LOOKING SCARED.

354
00:14:18,324 --> 00:14:19,758
Tyra: KAHLEN BROKE DOWN.

355
00:14:19,758 --> 00:14:22,194
NOBODY HAS THE RIGHT TO TREAT
ANYONE LIKE THAT.

356
00:14:22,194 --> 00:14:23,562
Tyra: NAIMA REMAINED CALM.

357
00:14:23,562 --> 00:14:25,864
I HAD TO LAUGH AT THIS GUY.

358
00:14:25,864 --> 00:14:29,335
Tyra: AND BRANDY,
SHE TOOK IT OUT ON TATIANA.

359
00:14:29,335 --> 00:14:31,503
I WAS MAKING A JOKE TO MAKE
MYSELF LAUGH.

360
00:14:31,503 --> 00:14:32,805
DON'T SAY NOTHING TO ME.

361
00:14:32,805 --> 00:14:34,606
IF WE DIDN'T GET KICKED OFF
FOR HITTING SOMEBODY,

362
00:14:34,606 --> 00:14:36,175
YOUR ASS WOULD BE
TORE UP RIGHT NOW,

363
00:14:36,175 --> 00:14:37,943
'CAUSE I DIDN'T SAY -- TO YOU.

364
00:14:37,943 --> 00:14:39,845
I REALLY DON'T SEE BRANDY
WORKING ON HER ATTITUDE

365
00:14:39,845 --> 00:14:42,114
OR HER TACT RIGHT NOW,
WHICH IS SAD.

366
00:14:42,114 --> 00:14:43,949
THE JUDGES
GAVE HER ANOTHER CHANCE,

367
00:14:43,949 --> 00:14:45,718
AND I DON'T THINK
SHE'S USING THAT.

368
00:14:45,718 --> 00:14:49,121
Tyra: HER ATTITUDE SPILLED OVER
INTO THE ZODIAC PHOTO SHOOT,

369
00:14:49,121 --> 00:14:50,989
WHERE BRANDY COULDN'T
STOP COMPLAINING.

370
00:14:50,989 --> 00:14:53,092
SO I'M LIKE THE LONGEST ONE,
HUH?

371
00:14:53,092 --> 00:14:54,259
Jay: WELL, YEAH.

372
00:14:54,259 --> 00:14:55,894
I'M ABOUT TO FALL.

373
00:14:55,894 --> 00:14:58,397
Jay: NO, YOU'RE NOT,
YOU'RE NOT GOING ANYWHERE.

374
00:14:58,397 --> 00:15:00,799
♪♪♪

375
00:15:00,799 --> 00:15:03,869
THERE'S SOMETHING ABOUT
THE PHOTO AND THE FACE--

376
00:15:03,869 --> 00:15:05,404
THERE'S SOMETHING
I'M NOT FEELING.

377
00:15:05,404 --> 00:15:06,905
THERE'S NO PASSION IN THE EYES.

378
00:15:06,905 --> 00:15:08,240
THE PHOTOGRAPHER THERE
WAS LIKE,

379
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:10,743
"OKAY, GIVE ME SEXY, OKAY,
WAIT A MINUTE, TOO SEXY.

380
00:15:10,743 --> 00:15:12,311
MOVE TO THE LEFT,
MOVE TO THE RIGHT, SO..."

381
00:15:12,311 --> 00:15:13,679
BRANDY, HAVE YOU HAD OTHER JOBS.

382
00:15:13,679 --> 00:15:14,947
LIKE, HOW MANY OTHER JOBS
HAVE YOU HAD?

383
00:15:14,947 --> 00:15:16,648
I THINK I HAD LIKE FOUR JOBS.

384
00:15:16,648 --> 00:15:18,117
SO FOUR JOBS MEANS FOUR BOSSES.

385
00:15:18,117 --> 00:15:20,519
AND FOUR BOSSES WITH FOUR
DIFFERENT TYPES OF STYLE

386
00:15:20,519 --> 00:15:22,454
OF HOW THEY DEAL
WITH THEIR EMPLOYEES.

387
00:15:22,454 --> 00:15:23,856
SAME WITH PHOTOGRAPHERS.

388
00:15:23,856 --> 00:15:25,958
THERE'S DIFFERENT PERSONALITIES,
AND YOU HAVE TO FIGURE OUT

389
00:15:25,958 --> 00:15:27,993
HOW TO HANDLE ALL OF THEM
IN A DIFFERENT WAY.

390
00:15:27,993 --> 00:15:31,296
IN THE END, THE JUDGES COULDN'T
GET PAST BRANDY'S ATTITUDE.

391
00:15:31,296 --> 00:15:32,598
THANK YOU, BRANDY.

392
00:15:32,598 --> 00:15:34,767
SO THEY SENT HER HOME.

393
00:15:37,102 --> 00:15:39,972
BEING A TOP MODEL MEANS
BEING AWAY FROM YOUR FAMILY.

394
00:15:39,972 --> 00:15:42,274
AND NOELLE HAD THE HARDEST TIME.

395
00:15:42,274 --> 00:15:43,642
HEY, BABY BOY.

396
00:15:43,642 --> 00:15:45,811
(baby talk on phone)

397
00:15:45,811 --> 00:15:48,347
KISSY, KISSY, KISSY, MWAH.

398
00:15:48,347 --> 00:15:50,182
IT'S REALLY LIKE AN
INDESCRIBABLE FEELING WHEN

399
00:15:50,182 --> 00:15:52,584
YOU FEEL LIKE YOU'RE MISSING
LITERALLY A PART OF YOURSELF.

400
00:15:52,584 --> 00:15:54,353
I KNOW SHE'S A PROUD MOTHER

401
00:15:54,353 --> 00:15:58,957
BUT NOELLE TALKS CONSTANTLY
ABOUT HER CHILD 24/7.

402
00:15:58,957 --> 00:16:01,393
MY BODY MATURED A LOT
FROM HAVING A BABY.

403
00:16:01,393 --> 00:16:02,928
ONCE YOU HAVE A BABY...

404
00:16:02,928 --> 00:16:05,697
MY SON WAS TAKING A NAP
FOR A GOOD HOUR AND A HALF.

405
00:16:05,697 --> 00:16:07,366
THAT'S THE DAY AFTER
HE WAS BORN,

406
00:16:07,366 --> 00:16:09,101
LOOK HOW PERFECT
HE LOOKS ALREADY.

407
00:16:09,101 --> 00:16:12,504
I LOVE MY BABY, I MISS MY BABY,
I WANNA TALK TO MY BABY.

408
00:16:12,504 --> 00:16:14,039
OH, YEAH.

409
00:16:14,039 --> 00:16:17,409
OKAY, WE GOT IT,
YOU HAVE A KID, NEXT.

410
00:16:17,409 --> 00:16:21,113
Tyra: WHEN MICHELLE WOKE UP WITH
OPEN SORES ALL OVER HER FACE,

411
00:16:21,113 --> 00:16:24,850
NOELLE'S THOUGHTS TURNED
FROM HER BABY TO HER SAFETY.

412
00:16:24,850 --> 00:16:26,118
THAT'S NOT A BUG BITE.

413
00:16:26,118 --> 00:16:28,787
IT LOOKS LIKE SHE'S PUTTING OUT
CIGARETTES ON HER FACE.

414
00:16:28,787 --> 00:16:29,955
I WANNA KNOW ABOUT IT

415
00:16:29,955 --> 00:16:31,957
'CAUSE I DON'T WANT THAT
TO HAPPEN TO MY FACE.

416
00:16:31,957 --> 00:16:34,560
THERE IS SOME STRAIN
OF BACTERIA

417
00:16:34,560 --> 00:16:37,029
THAT IS RESISTANT
TO ANTIBIOTICS.

418
00:16:37,029 --> 00:16:39,698
YOU CAN GET PNEUMONIA AND DIE
FROM THE PNEUMONIA.

419
00:16:39,698 --> 00:16:41,200
OH!

420
00:16:41,200 --> 00:16:43,502
IT HAS BEEN ALL OVER
THE MEDIA THAT THERE IS A NEW

421
00:16:43,502 --> 00:16:47,606
FLESH-EATING BACTERIA THAT IS
UNCURABLE BY ANTIBIOTICS.

422
00:16:47,606 --> 00:16:50,108
Tyra: AND AN ITCHING EPIDEMIC
EXPLODED.

423
00:16:50,108 --> 00:16:51,510
WHAT!

424
00:16:53,779 --> 00:16:55,147
WHOO, I'M ITCHY.

425
00:16:57,950 --> 00:16:59,451
WE'RE ALL GONNA DIE!

426
00:17:01,620 --> 00:17:04,256
Tyra: WHILE MICHELLE VISITED
A DERMATOLOGIST...

427
00:17:04,256 --> 00:17:05,657
Man: HAVE YOU EVER
HEARD OF IMPETIGO?

428
00:17:05,657 --> 00:17:07,359
NO.

429
00:17:07,359 --> 00:17:10,596
IT'S USUALLY CAUSED BY BACTERIA
AND IT'S EASILY TREATABLE,

430
00:17:10,596 --> 00:17:12,564
AND PROBABLY WILL GO AWAY
FAIRLY QUICKLY.

431
00:17:12,564 --> 00:17:13,866
THANK YOU, I APPRECIATE IT.

432
00:17:13,866 --> 00:17:15,200
YOU'RE WELCOME.

433
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:17,469
Tyra: THE GIRLS FACED
A COMPLEX PHOTO SHOOT

434
00:17:17,469 --> 00:17:19,304
WHERE THEY HAD TO PORTRAY
DIFFERENT ETHNICITIES

435
00:17:19,304 --> 00:17:22,274
WHILE JUGGLING A GLASS OF MILK
AND A HEAVY TODDLER.

436
00:17:27,179 --> 00:17:28,313
HE'S SLIDING.

437
00:17:30,482 --> 00:17:33,385
- I'M JUST SLIPPING DOWN.
- YOU ARE SLIPPING, HUH?

438
00:17:37,356 --> 00:17:39,758
Man: DON'T PULL OUT HER HAT.

439
00:17:39,758 --> 00:17:41,693
DO YOU HAVE GUM?

440
00:17:41,693 --> 00:17:43,228
NO, I DON'T HAVE ANY GUM,
SWEETIE.

441
00:17:43,228 --> 00:17:45,631
HIGH FIVE, ALL RIGHT.

442
00:17:45,631 --> 00:17:48,400
Tyra: MICHELLE RETURNED
WITH THE DOCTOR'S APPROVAL.

443
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:51,937
IT'LL CLEAR UP, IT'S CONTAGIOUS.

444
00:17:51,937 --> 00:17:54,673
Tyra: BUT SHE WASN'T ALLOWED
TO POSE WITH A TODDLER.

445
00:17:54,673 --> 00:17:56,909
YOU NEED TO BOND
WITH YOUR CHILD.

446
00:17:56,909 --> 00:17:58,610
HE'S NOT GONNA BEHAVE
LIKE THE REST OF 'EM.

447
00:17:58,610 --> 00:18:00,579
Tyra: AND SOME OF THE GIRLS
THOUGHT THIS WAS UNFAIR.

448
00:18:00,579 --> 00:18:02,714
OKAY, WILL SHE BEAT US
AT THIS CHALLENGE?

449
00:18:02,714 --> 00:18:05,117
NO, WE DON'T, WE WANNA GO PUT
SOME WEIGHTS IN THE THING.

450
00:18:07,452 --> 00:18:09,087
IT'S NOT A SORORITY.

451
00:18:09,087 --> 00:18:12,257
THIS IS A MODELING COMPETITION.

452
00:18:12,257 --> 00:18:14,760
♪♪♪

453
00:18:16,728 --> 00:18:18,063
IT WAS LIGHT.

454
00:18:18,063 --> 00:18:19,998
SHE COMES OUT OF THE SHOOT
AND SAYS,

455
00:18:19,998 --> 00:18:22,601
"WHOO, YEAH, I ONLY HAD
A HALF-POUND BABY."

456
00:18:22,601 --> 00:18:24,803
I WANT TO TAKE THAT DARK WIG OFF
MICHELLE'S HEAD AND SAY,

457
00:18:24,803 --> 00:18:27,172
"YOU'RE RIGHT, YOU ONLY HAD
A HALF-POUND BABY BECAUSE

458
00:18:27,172 --> 00:18:29,308
"YOU SCRATCHED YOUR FACE,
YOU GOT BACTERIA ON YOUR FACE

459
00:18:29,308 --> 00:18:31,810
AND NOW YOU'RE NOT CAPABLE."

460
00:18:31,810 --> 00:18:34,413
Tyra: BUT IN THE END IT WAS
NOELLE WHO DIDN'T MEASURE UP.

461
00:18:34,413 --> 00:18:36,715
NOELLE, THE JUDGES SEE YOU
AND THEY SAY,

462
00:18:36,715 --> 00:18:39,017
"SHE DOESN'T REALLY LOOK
LIKE A MODEL IN PERSON."

463
00:18:39,017 --> 00:18:40,852
AND SHE WAS SENT HOME.

464
00:18:40,852 --> 00:18:42,154
Noelle:
THE PERSON I PERSONALLY THINK

465
00:18:42,154 --> 00:18:44,590
SHOULD'VE GONE HOME
WAS MICHELLE.

466
00:18:44,590 --> 00:18:47,059
THAT SOFT, SILENT, SWEET LITTLE
ATTITUDE THAT YOU PUT ON

467
00:18:47,059 --> 00:18:50,529
FOR THE JUDGES,
ISN'T REALLY WHO YOU ARE.

468
00:18:50,529 --> 00:18:52,798
AND SOONER OR LATER,
THAT'LL COME OUT.

469
00:19:00,205 --> 00:19:02,274
Tyra: THE PRESSURE OF
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL"

470
00:19:02,274 --> 00:19:04,476
AFFECTS EACH GIRL
IN A DIFFERENT WAY.

471
00:19:04,476 --> 00:19:07,346
SOME GIRLS TURN SILLY...

472
00:19:07,346 --> 00:19:09,481
OH, YOU ASS.

473
00:19:09,481 --> 00:19:10,782
SHUT THE DOOR!
SHUT THE DOOR!

474
00:19:10,782 --> 00:19:13,285
SHUT THE DOOR.

475
00:19:13,285 --> 00:19:16,421
THERE'S NOWHERE TO HIDE,
THERE'S NOWHERE TO HIDE!

476
00:19:16,421 --> 00:19:17,489
I DON'T KNOW!

477
00:19:17,489 --> 00:19:19,558
GET HER!

478
00:19:19,558 --> 00:19:22,661
- ALL RIGHT, TRUCE?
- TRUCE.

479
00:19:22,661 --> 00:19:24,162
Tyra: SOME GIRLS SHUT DOWN.

480
00:19:24,162 --> 00:19:26,932
(crickets chirping)

481
00:19:26,932 --> 00:19:30,669
(owl hooting)

482
00:19:30,669 --> 00:19:33,071
AND SOME HANDLE THE STRESS
BY GOING WILD.

483
00:19:35,774 --> 00:19:36,908
AND WILD...

484
00:19:39,011 --> 00:19:40,646
AND WILD.

485
00:19:40,646 --> 00:19:42,481
I THINK THAT I AM DEFINITELY
THE ENTERTAINMENT.

486
00:19:42,481 --> 00:19:44,950
WHAT ARE THEY GONNA DO
WITHOUT ME IF I LEAVE?

487
00:19:44,950 --> 00:19:47,252
WHOO! WHOA.

488
00:19:47,252 --> 00:19:48,987
THERE'S NEVER A DULL MOMENT
WITH THAT GIRL.

489
00:19:48,987 --> 00:19:51,256
RIGHT HERE, GO FOR IT.

490
00:19:51,256 --> 00:19:52,424
THERE YOU GO.

491
00:19:52,424 --> 00:19:56,228
♪♪♪

492
00:19:56,228 --> 00:19:58,664
PUT YOUR FEET THIS WAY.

493
00:19:58,664 --> 00:20:00,232
PUT YOUR HEAD BACK THIS WAY,
COME HERE.

494
00:20:00,232 --> 00:20:01,633
RIGHT THERE.

495
00:20:01,633 --> 00:20:03,835
IF ANYTHING, BRITTANY IS HAVING
A LITTLE BIT TOO MUCH FUN.

496
00:20:06,805 --> 00:20:08,040
Tyra: AT A COVER GIRL PARTY,

497
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:10,909
THE GIRLS WORKED TO IMPRESS
INDUSTRY INSIDERS.

498
00:20:15,447 --> 00:20:18,283
IT FEELS LIKE I'M DREAMING AND
I'M GONNA WAKE UP ANY DAY NOW?

499
00:20:18,283 --> 00:20:19,818
Tyra: WHILE THE OTHER GIRLS
WORKED THE ROOM,

500
00:20:19,818 --> 00:20:21,820
BRITTANY WAS BUSY
WORKING ON A BUZZ.

501
00:20:21,820 --> 00:20:23,822
HOLD ON, DRINKS!

502
00:20:23,822 --> 00:20:25,357
BRITTANY, SHE WANTED A DRINK

503
00:20:25,357 --> 00:20:27,626
AND SHE WAS GONNA HAVE A DRINK
AND THAT WAS ALL.

504
00:20:27,626 --> 00:20:29,795
BRITTANY,
THEY WERE A LITTLE CONCERNED.

505
00:20:29,795 --> 00:20:32,597
THEY THOUGHT YOUR PRIORITY WAS
MORE ABOUT YOUR DRINKING

506
00:20:32,597 --> 00:20:35,033
THAN MEETING EVERYBODY
AT THE PARTY.

507
00:20:35,033 --> 00:20:37,602
NO ONE WANTS TO HEAR
NEGATIVE FEEDBACK, IT'S HURTFUL.

508
00:20:37,602 --> 00:20:39,504
IT'S VERY NERVE-WRACKING.

509
00:20:39,504 --> 00:20:40,906
Tyra: FEELING OVERWHELMED,

510
00:20:40,906 --> 00:20:43,608
BRITTANY TURNED TO HER ROOMMATE
KEENYAH AND FOUND A FRIEND.

511
00:20:43,608 --> 00:20:45,477
I REALLY THINK YOU'RE SPECIAL.

512
00:20:45,477 --> 00:20:47,913
IF I'M IN A ROOM AND YOU'RE
NOT AROUND, IT'S LIKE...

513
00:20:47,913 --> 00:20:50,348
WHERE'S BRITTANY?

514
00:20:50,348 --> 00:20:52,884
YOU HAVE PRESENCE,
I FEEL LIKE THE ROOM IS FULL.

515
00:20:52,884 --> 00:20:54,286
IT CAN BE JUST ME AND YOU,

516
00:20:54,286 --> 00:20:56,188
AND IT WILL FEEL LIKE
EVERYBODY HERE.

517
00:20:56,188 --> 00:20:57,556
THANK YOU A LOT.

518
00:20:57,556 --> 00:20:59,624
I JUST CAN'T--
HOW MUCH I LOVE YOU!

519
00:20:59,624 --> 00:21:01,526
OH.

520
00:21:01,526 --> 00:21:02,594
Tyra: AT THE NEXT PHOTO SHOOT,

521
00:21:02,594 --> 00:21:04,763
THE GIRLS HAD TO BRAVE
THE ELEMENTS.

522
00:21:04,763 --> 00:21:07,799
♪♪♪

523
00:21:11,403 --> 00:21:13,939
A DETERMINED BRITTANY,
BLEW JAY AWAY.

524
00:21:13,939 --> 00:21:17,375
Jay: SHE WAS VERY REMINISCENT
OF THE EARLY JANICE DICKINSON.

525
00:21:17,375 --> 00:21:18,910
SHE LOOKED GREAT.

526
00:21:18,910 --> 00:21:19,945
PULL UP!

527
00:21:19,945 --> 00:21:21,146
LLUVY, BE GRACEFUL.

528
00:21:21,146 --> 00:21:23,448
SMILE, SMILE, LAUGH!

529
00:21:23,448 --> 00:21:25,917
BUT LLUVY BRING HIM
CRASHING DOWN TO EARTH.

530
00:21:25,917 --> 00:21:29,087
OH, SHE LOOKS LIKE A DRAG QUEEN.

531
00:21:29,087 --> 00:21:31,156
YOU NEVER PLAYED SEXY
IN THE SHOWER, DID YOU?

532
00:21:31,156 --> 00:21:32,824
NEVER, EVER, EVER.

533
00:21:32,824 --> 00:21:35,327
GO HOME, PLAY SEXY
IN THE SHOWER.

534
00:21:35,327 --> 00:21:37,028
YOU HAVE THE WATER ON,
AND YOU FEEL LIKE

535
00:21:37,028 --> 00:21:39,397
YOU'RE THE HOTTEST THING
SINCE SLICED BREAD.

536
00:21:39,397 --> 00:21:40,532
YOU'RE A BEAUTIFUL GIRL.

537
00:21:40,532 --> 00:21:42,868
YOU NEED TO START
REALIZING THAT.

538
00:21:42,868 --> 00:21:44,436
Tyra: LLUVY HAD A UNIQUE BEAUTY,

539
00:21:44,436 --> 00:21:46,571
BUT SHE DIDN'T KNOW HOW TO PUT
THAT ON A PICTURE.

540
00:21:46,571 --> 00:21:48,106
SO IT WAS HER TURN TO GO HOME.

541
00:21:48,106 --> 00:21:49,307
Janice: TAKE CARE, DOLL.

542
00:21:49,307 --> 00:21:50,842
THANK YOU, GUYS.

543
00:21:54,746 --> 00:21:57,415
Tyra: HERE'S ANOTHER MOMENT
FROM THE "TOP MODEL" VAULT.

544
00:21:57,415 --> 00:21:59,785
YOU HAVE TO SELL YOUR PRODUCT
TO US.

545
00:21:59,785 --> 00:22:02,921
IT'S GOT A FRUITY SMELL,
AND, UM...

546
00:22:02,921 --> 00:22:05,657
IT'S...

547
00:22:07,793 --> 00:22:10,061
TATIANA.

548
00:22:10,061 --> 00:22:12,831
I...

549
00:22:12,831 --> 00:22:14,166
(chuckling)

550
00:22:14,166 --> 00:22:15,934
REALLY, UM...

551
00:22:15,934 --> 00:22:17,502
JUST HERE,
I DON'T KNOW WHAT TO SAY.

552
00:22:17,502 --> 00:22:18,537
THANK YOU.

553
00:22:18,537 --> 00:22:19,704
'CAUSE YOU DIDN'T KNOW
WHAT TO SAY.

554
00:22:19,704 --> 00:22:22,040
COMING UP,
TIFFANY TRIES SOMETHING NEW.

555
00:22:22,040 --> 00:22:23,208
SUSHI!

556
00:22:25,310 --> 00:22:27,546
AND SOME SPECIAL GUESTS
SURPRISE THE GIRLS.

557
00:22:27,546 --> 00:22:28,814
MY MOM IS HERE.

558
00:22:28,814 --> 00:22:33,251
WIND HER UP
AND WIND HER UP TIGHT.

559
00:22:35,754 --> 00:22:37,322
♪♪♪

560
00:22:37,322 --> 00:22:41,026
Tyra: BEING A TOP MODEL, MEANS
MANAGING MANY NEW EXPERIENCES.

561
00:22:41,026 --> 00:22:43,495
SOME GIRLS DEAL WITH THIS
BETTER THAN OTHERS.

562
00:22:43,495 --> 00:22:46,731
SUSHI!

563
00:22:46,731 --> 00:22:49,034
I'M NOT USED
TO EATING RAW STUFF.

564
00:22:49,034 --> 00:22:51,269
I'M USED TO HAVING IT COOKED
OR BURNT OR SOMETHING.

565
00:22:53,972 --> 00:22:56,541
HERE, TRY THAT ONE.

566
00:22:56,541 --> 00:22:58,476
TRY THAT, TRY THAT.

567
00:22:58,476 --> 00:23:00,512
TRY THIS WITHOUT THE SKIN,
JUST TRY IT.

568
00:23:02,681 --> 00:23:05,417
TIFFANY, SHE DOESN'T EAT A LOT
WHEN WE GOT OUT BECAUSE

569
00:23:05,417 --> 00:23:06,918
SHE'S JUST LIKE REALLY
NOT USED TO THE FOOD,

570
00:23:06,918 --> 00:23:08,453
AND SHE REALLY DOESN'T LIKE IT.

571
00:23:10,889 --> 00:23:14,459
THIS WHOLE EXPERIENCE IS TOTALLY
DIFFERENT FROM ANYTHING

572
00:23:14,459 --> 00:23:16,494
I'VE EVER BEEN IN MY WHOLE LIFE.

573
00:23:16,494 --> 00:23:18,396
AND IT FEELS LIKE
EVERYBODY ELSE

574
00:23:18,396 --> 00:23:20,999
IS A LITTLE BIT MORE
COMFORTABLE THAN ME.

575
00:23:22,901 --> 00:23:24,703
Tyra: AS IF EATING FOREIGN FOOD
WASN'T ENOUGH,

576
00:23:24,703 --> 00:23:27,906
NEXT TIFFANY HAD TO LEARN
A FOREIGN WAY OF SPEAKING.

577
00:23:27,906 --> 00:23:30,308
AS MODELS, YOU'LL BE CALLED
ON TO HAVE A LOT

578
00:23:30,308 --> 00:23:32,510
IN YOUR BAG OF TRICKS.

579
00:23:32,510 --> 00:23:36,514
I'M GOING TO TEACH YOU
A DIALECT: COCKNEY.

580
00:23:36,514 --> 00:23:39,251
COCKNEY?
I CAN BARELY SPEAK ENGLISH.

581
00:23:39,251 --> 00:23:41,586
Tyra: TO TOP IT OFF,
SHE HAD TO USE THE ACCENT

582
00:23:41,586 --> 00:23:44,322
IN A SCENE WITH SEXY ACTOR
BORIS KODJOE.

583
00:23:44,322 --> 00:23:47,025
WHAT?!
OH NO!

584
00:23:48,727 --> 00:23:50,795
IT'S NOT ONE OF THOSE SCENES

585
00:23:50,795 --> 00:23:52,864
WHERE I COULD BE CUTE
AROUND BORIS.

586
00:23:52,864 --> 00:23:55,667
I HAVE TO HAVE
A DAMN MISSING TOOTH

587
00:23:55,667 --> 00:23:57,769
RIGHT IN THE MIDDLE OF MY MOUTH.

588
00:23:57,769 --> 00:24:00,372
(laughing)

589
00:24:00,372 --> 00:24:02,274
WELL, HELLO THERE, GOVERNOR.

590
00:24:02,274 --> 00:24:05,443
- LOVELY DAY, ISN'T IT?
- I HAVEN'T NOTICED.

591
00:24:05,443 --> 00:24:07,612
WELL, THE SUN'S SHINNING.

592
00:24:07,612 --> 00:24:10,982
THE SKY'S SPARKLING BLUE.

593
00:24:13,285 --> 00:24:17,222
I CAN'T REMEMBER NO STUPIDNESS
LIKE ENGLISH COCKNEY?

594
00:24:17,222 --> 00:24:19,124
I'M REALLY EMBARRASSED.

595
00:24:19,124 --> 00:24:22,160
MAYBE I CAN'T BE THIS PERSON
THAT-- THIS MODEL GIRL THAN

596
00:24:22,160 --> 00:24:23,728
MAYBE THAT'S NOT WHO I AM.

597
00:24:23,728 --> 00:24:26,464
Tyra: FRUSTRATED BY
THE COMPETITION,

598
00:24:26,464 --> 00:24:28,199
TIFFANY CALLED HER GRANDMOTHER
TO VENT.

599
00:24:28,199 --> 00:24:30,268
I CAN'T TAKE SOMEBODY
LOOKING DOWN ON ME,

600
00:24:30,268 --> 00:24:32,103
TRYING TO MAKE ME FEEL
LIKE I'M LESS OF MYSELF.

601
00:24:32,103 --> 00:24:34,339
SO I REALIZED, I'MA BE THE BEST
TIFFANY I CAN BE.

602
00:24:34,339 --> 00:24:35,573
THEY EITHER LOVE IT OR DON'T.

603
00:24:35,573 --> 00:24:38,843
THIS IS SOMETHING THAT
YOU HAVE TO GO THROUGH.

604
00:24:38,843 --> 00:24:41,947
YOU AIN'T NO QUITTER,
YOU ARE A FIGHTER.

605
00:24:41,947 --> 00:24:43,014
I'M NOT GONNA QUIT.

606
00:24:45,417 --> 00:24:46,518
Tyra:
AT THE PHOTO SHOOT,

607
00:24:46,518 --> 00:24:47,919
IT WAS REBECCA'S TURN
TO STRUGGLE.

608
00:24:50,088 --> 00:24:51,089
YES.

609
00:24:51,089 --> 00:24:52,791
Rebecca:
OH, JEEZ, I'M NOT EXCITED

610
00:24:52,791 --> 00:24:54,059
LIKE SOME OF THE GIRLS HERE.

611
00:24:54,059 --> 00:24:55,927
I'M ENGAGED AND ABOUT TO BE
MARRIED WHEN I GET HOME

612
00:24:55,927 --> 00:24:57,462
SO IT'S A LITTLE AWKWARD.

613
00:24:57,462 --> 00:25:00,065
OKAY, NOW THE ESTROGEN'S
REALLY FLOWING.

614
00:25:00,065 --> 00:25:01,366
WE'RE HORNY.

615
00:25:01,366 --> 00:25:02,767
CAN I BE FIRST? RIGHT HERE,
RIGHT HERE, I'M READY.

616
00:25:02,767 --> 00:25:04,302
WORK IT OUT!

617
00:25:04,302 --> 00:25:05,737
OH, GOOD GIRL!

618
00:25:05,737 --> 00:25:07,772
BRITTANY, ACT OUT!

619
00:25:07,772 --> 00:25:10,108
HOLD THAT PILLOW, GIRL,
HOLD THAT PILLOW.

620
00:25:10,108 --> 00:25:12,210
DON'T BE AFRAID OF HIM.

621
00:25:12,210 --> 00:25:14,045
WHOO!

622
00:25:14,045 --> 00:25:16,915
- COME ON, LAUGH AT HIM.
- COME ON, TIFFANY.

623
00:25:16,915 --> 00:25:18,183
I SEE THIS IS MY TEST.

624
00:25:18,183 --> 00:25:19,284
IF I CAN PULL THIS OFF,
THEN GREAT,

625
00:25:19,284 --> 00:25:20,885
I HOPE I'LL GET TO STICK AROUND.

626
00:25:20,885 --> 00:25:23,154
BUT I'M--
I'M REALLY TERRIFIED.

627
00:25:23,154 --> 00:25:27,792
- HIT HIM!
- LOOK AT HIM!

628
00:25:27,792 --> 00:25:29,494
THERE YOU GO!

629
00:25:29,494 --> 00:25:31,396
I DON'T KNOW IF I HAVE A PICTURE

630
00:25:31,396 --> 00:25:32,630
THE JUDGES ARE GONNA
BE HAPPY WITH.

631
00:25:32,630 --> 00:25:34,399
I'VE NEVER WALKED AWAY
FROM ANY PHOTO SHOOT

632
00:25:34,399 --> 00:25:36,801
GOING, "YES, I NAILED IT."
I DON'T KNOW.

633
00:25:36,801 --> 00:25:39,704
I THINK WE ALL GOT HAIR BALLED.

634
00:25:39,838 --> 00:25:42,007
Tyra: FOR THE JUDGING CHALLENGE,
THE GIRLS HAD TO PUT

635
00:25:42,007 --> 00:25:43,575
THEIR NEW ACTING SKILLS
TO THE TEST

636
00:25:43,575 --> 00:25:46,211
AND BECOME CORRESPONDENTS.

637
00:25:46,211 --> 00:25:47,445
EVERY GIRL STRUGGLED.

638
00:25:47,445 --> 00:25:50,048
HI, MICHELLE HERE.
IT'S FASHION WEEK IN PARIS.

639
00:25:50,048 --> 00:25:52,283
CAN YOU SAY...

640
00:25:52,283 --> 00:25:54,185
- "MAGNETA?"
- MA-GEN-TA?

641
00:25:54,185 --> 00:25:55,887
"IZZY MI-E?"

642
00:25:55,887 --> 00:25:58,023
"ICY ME-AKE."

643
00:25:58,023 --> 00:26:01,926
LOOKS TO THE LEFT, WHOA.

644
00:26:01,926 --> 00:26:04,329
"AU REVOIR."

645
00:26:04,329 --> 00:26:07,198
Tyra: AND ONCE AGAIN,
TIFFANY GAVE UP ON HERSELF.

646
00:26:07,198 --> 00:26:08,600
I CAN'T DO THIS.

647
00:26:08,600 --> 00:26:11,002
TIFFANY, THE OTHER GIRLS
DID NOT KNOW THESE WORDS.

648
00:26:11,002 --> 00:26:13,838
JUST HAVE FUN WITH IT,
USE YOUR PERSONALITY, BE YOU.

649
00:26:16,808 --> 00:26:18,777
WHILE THE JUDGES DELIBERATED,

650
00:26:18,777 --> 00:26:21,713
TIFFANY SHARED HER FRUSTRATION
WITH THE OTHER GIRLS.

651
00:26:21,713 --> 00:26:23,181
I QUIT THE WHOLE THING.

652
00:26:23,181 --> 00:26:25,683
- OH, HOW DID IT GO?
- HORRIBLE.

653
00:26:25,683 --> 00:26:27,986
A PART OF ME KIND OF GAVE UP
ON THE INSIDE.

654
00:26:27,986 --> 00:26:30,288
SO I WASN'T BEING
THE BEST TIFFANY I CAN BE.

655
00:26:30,288 --> 00:26:32,057
EVERY WEEK,
I DO SOMETHING STUPID,

656
00:26:32,057 --> 00:26:33,324
I MESS UP WITH SOMETHING.

657
00:26:33,324 --> 00:26:35,927
THEY MAKING IT LIKE,
MAKING ME HATE THIS.

658
00:26:35,927 --> 00:26:38,229
DON'T WANNA SEEM LIKE
I'M UNGRATEFUL FOR BEING HERE.

659
00:26:38,229 --> 00:26:40,965
I LOVE BEING HERE,
BUT I WAS TIRED OF IT.

660
00:26:40,965 --> 00:26:42,934
I FEEL LIKE TODAY, I WANNA GO.

661
00:26:44,202 --> 00:26:45,670
TIFFANY WAS READY TO GO.

662
00:26:45,670 --> 00:26:48,740
BUT REBECCA WAS ABOUT TO HEAR
SOME HARD NEWS.

663
00:26:53,244 --> 00:26:55,180
BOTH OF YOU WILL PACK YOUR BAGS

664
00:26:55,180 --> 00:26:56,881
AND RETURN TO THE LOFT.

665
00:27:00,685 --> 00:27:03,488
BUT WHEN TIFFANY LAUGHED OFF
HER ELIMINATION,

666
00:27:03,488 --> 00:27:06,157
I GOT FRUSTRATED
WITH HER ATTITUDE.

667
00:27:06,157 --> 00:27:09,727
TIFFANY, I'M EXTREMELY
DISAPPOINTED IN YOU.

668
00:27:09,727 --> 00:27:11,463
THIS IS A JOKE TO YOU.

669
00:27:11,463 --> 00:27:13,231
I'M HURT, BUT EVERY TIME
I COME HERE,

670
00:27:13,231 --> 00:27:14,499
IT'S, "OH, YOU HAVE
A BAD ATTITUDE."

671
00:27:14,499 --> 00:27:15,700
I DON'T HAVE A BAD ATTITUDE.

672
00:27:15,700 --> 00:27:17,602
MAYBE I AM ANGRY INSIDE.

673
00:27:17,602 --> 00:27:19,204
I'VE BEEN THROUGH STUFF
SO I'M ANGRY.

674
00:27:19,204 --> 00:27:21,940
YES, BUT DOES NOT--
THIS IS NOT-- BE QUIET, TIFFANY.

675
00:27:21,940 --> 00:27:24,209
BE QUIET!
THAT IS WHAT'S WRONG WITH YOU.

676
00:27:24,209 --> 00:27:25,243
STOP IT!

677
00:27:27,512 --> 00:27:30,715
I HAVE NEVER IN MY LIFE
YELLED AT A GIRL LIKE THIS!

678
00:27:30,715 --> 00:27:33,218
I WAS ROOTING FOR YOU.

679
00:27:33,218 --> 00:27:35,153
LEARN SOMETHING FROM THIS!

680
00:27:35,153 --> 00:27:36,554
WHEN YOU GO TO BED AT NIGHT,

681
00:27:36,554 --> 00:27:39,057
YOU LAY THERE AND YOU TAKE
RESPONSIBILITY FOR YOURSELF,

682
00:27:39,057 --> 00:27:41,726
BECAUSE NOBODY'S GOING TO TAKE
RESPONSIBILITY FOR YOU.

683
00:27:41,726 --> 00:27:43,361
YOU'RE ROLLING YOUR EYES

684
00:27:43,361 --> 00:27:45,396
AND YOU ACT LIKE IT'S BECAUSE
YOU'VE HEARD IT ALL BEFORE.

685
00:27:45,396 --> 00:27:48,466
TAKE RESPONSIBILITY
FOR YOURSELF.

686
00:27:51,970 --> 00:27:53,805
ANYBODY ELSE'LL TELL ME
TO SHUT UP,

687
00:27:53,805 --> 00:27:55,006
I WOULD'VE SLAPPED THEM.

688
00:27:55,006 --> 00:27:57,542
BUT SHE WAS RIGHT 'CAUSE
SHE COULD'VE EASILY SAID,

689
00:27:57,542 --> 00:27:59,077
"OKAY, WHATEVER, YOU KNOW, BYE."

690
00:27:59,077 --> 00:28:01,746
THAT SHOWED ME THAT SHE SAW
DEEPLY INTO ME.

691
00:28:01,746 --> 00:28:03,681
SHE CARED ABOUT ME

692
00:28:03,681 --> 00:28:05,150
AND THAT'S COOL KNOWING THAT,
YOU KNOW,

693
00:28:05,150 --> 00:28:06,451
TYRA CARES ABOUT YOU.

694
00:28:06,451 --> 00:28:08,720
I HAVE THE UTMOST
RESPECT FOR HER.

695
00:28:08,720 --> 00:28:12,023
I'M GONNA GO BACK HOME
AND HAVE A GOOD LIFE NOW

696
00:28:12,023 --> 00:28:14,092
AND BE THE BEST TIFFANY
I CAN BE.

697
00:28:14,092 --> 00:28:16,227
Rebecca: I'M REALLY
DISAPPOINTED RIGHT NOW.

698
00:28:16,227 --> 00:28:18,429
BUT I'M GOING HOME
TO GET MARRIED.

699
00:28:18,429 --> 00:28:20,198
AND WE'LL TAKE IT FROM THERE.

700
00:28:20,198 --> 00:28:23,468
♪♪♪

701
00:28:26,938 --> 00:28:29,274
Tatiana: WHEN TYRA WAS YELLING
AT TIFFANY,

702
00:28:29,274 --> 00:28:32,243
I UNDERSTOOD, LIKE,
WHERE SHE WAS COMING FROM

703
00:28:32,243 --> 00:28:34,245
BECAUSE, YOU KNOW, TYRA IS
REALLY PASSIONATE.

704
00:28:34,245 --> 00:28:36,481
SO TODAY,
WE'RE KIND OF FEELING LIKE,

705
00:28:36,481 --> 00:28:38,516
WOW, WE NEED TO MOVE IT UP
A LITTLE BIT.

706
00:28:38,516 --> 00:28:40,084
OH, BABY.

707
00:28:40,084 --> 00:28:42,587
Tyra: THE NEXT DAY, THE GIRLS
GOT A LESSON IN INTERVIEWING

708
00:28:42,587 --> 00:28:44,789
FROM "ENTERTAINMENT TONIGHT'S"
JANN CARL.

709
00:28:44,789 --> 00:28:47,592
I AM HERE TODAY
TO TEACH YOU HOW TO ACT

710
00:28:47,592 --> 00:28:49,994
WHEN YOU ARE THROWN INTO
THE MEDIA SPOTLIGHT.

711
00:28:49,994 --> 00:28:52,263
Tyra: CHRISTINA AND TATIANA
LEARNED THAT THEY NEEDED

712
00:28:52,263 --> 00:28:54,165
TO EXPAND THEIR VOCABULARY.

713
00:28:54,165 --> 00:28:55,833
HI, I'M CHRISTINA WITH
"ENTERTAINMENT TONIGHT."

714
00:28:55,833 --> 00:28:56,901
AND WE ARE ACTUALLY HERE

715
00:28:56,901 --> 00:28:59,037
WITH "AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL",
TATIANA.

716
00:28:59,037 --> 00:29:00,605
ACTUALLY,
I HAVE A FEW QUESTIONS FOR YOU.

717
00:29:00,605 --> 00:29:03,875
UM, ACTUALLY, I WAS WONDERING,
HAS THERE BEEN ANY DESIGNERS

718
00:29:03,875 --> 00:29:06,544
OR ANY MODELS THAT HAVE INSPIRED
YOU OR ANY FAMILY MEMBERS?

719
00:29:06,544 --> 00:29:08,546
ACTUALLY, UM, MY COUSIN.

720
00:29:08,546 --> 00:29:11,649
HE'S ACTUALLY, YOU KNOW,
ALWAYS PUSHED ME AND PUSHED ME

721
00:29:11,649 --> 00:29:12,784
AND MYSELF,

722
00:29:12,784 --> 00:29:15,086
I PUSH MYSELF A LOT, ACTUALLY.

723
00:29:15,086 --> 00:29:17,222
Christina:
IT'S A LOT MORE DIFFICULT
THAN YOU ACTUALLY THINK IT IS.

724
00:29:17,222 --> 00:29:20,058
SO I'M GLAD WE HAD
THE EXPERIENCE, ACTUALLY.

725
00:29:20,191 --> 00:29:22,227
Tyra: CHRISTINA AND TATIANA
TANKED AT THE LESSON,

726
00:29:22,227 --> 00:29:24,262
BUT MADE A MAJOR COMEBACK
AT THE CHALLENGE

727
00:29:24,262 --> 00:29:26,564
WITH RAPPER,
ACTRESS, DESIGNER, EVE.

728
00:29:26,564 --> 00:29:27,665
WHERE DID YOU GET
THE NAME "FETISH" FROM?

729
00:29:27,665 --> 00:29:29,067
WHERE DID YOU COME UP WITH THAT?

730
00:29:29,067 --> 00:29:31,169
AND IF YOU COULD SUM UP YOUR
LINE AS FAR AS ATTITUDE-WISE

731
00:29:31,169 --> 00:29:33,238
IN ONE WORD,
WHAT WOULD IT BE?

732
00:29:33,238 --> 00:29:35,106
HMM... THAT'S HARD.

733
00:29:35,807 --> 00:29:37,842
HELLO AGAIN.

734
00:29:37,842 --> 00:29:40,478
Tyra: TATIANA THOUGHT THAT SHE
HAD THE COMPETITION IN THE BAG.

735
00:29:40,478 --> 00:29:43,781
BUT THE WINNER OF THE CHALLENGE
IS CHRISTINA.

736
00:29:43,781 --> 00:29:45,183
OH, THANK YOU.

737
00:29:45,183 --> 00:29:46,951
Tatiana: I THOUGHT I DID
A REALLY GOOD JOB.

738
00:29:46,951 --> 00:29:50,388
AND SO I'M JUST LIKE
KIND OF BUMMED A LITTLE BIT.

739
00:29:50,388 --> 00:29:51,422
THERE'S SOMETHING ELSE

740
00:29:51,422 --> 00:29:53,091
THAT COMES WITH WINNING
THIS CHALLENGE,

741
00:29:53,091 --> 00:29:55,059
BUT YOU HAVE TO PICK A FRIEND
TO ENJOY IT WITH.

742
00:29:55,059 --> 00:29:56,894
BRITTANY.

743
00:29:56,894 --> 00:29:58,329
YEAH!

744
00:29:58,329 --> 00:30:00,999
Tyra: THEIR PRIZE WAS A VISIT
FROM SOME SPECIAL GUESTS.

745
00:30:00,999 --> 00:30:02,133
BRITTANY!

746
00:30:02,133 --> 00:30:06,371
- (screaming)
- OH MY-- OH MY GOD!

747
00:30:06,371 --> 00:30:08,406
I CAN'T BELIEVE MY MOM IS HERE.

748
00:30:08,406 --> 00:30:10,608
- (screaming)
- MY MOM!

749
00:30:10,608 --> 00:30:11,943
I WAS LIKE, WHERE'S MY MOM?

750
00:30:11,943 --> 00:30:13,177
AND THEN I REMEMBERED,

751
00:30:13,177 --> 00:30:16,114
BRITTANY AND CHRISTINA WON
THE CHALLENGE, SO...

752
00:30:16,114 --> 00:30:17,649
ONLY THEIR MOMMIES ARE HERE.

753
00:30:17,649 --> 00:30:19,684
WE CAN PRETEND
WE'RE YOU'RE MAMAS.

754
00:30:19,684 --> 00:30:20,718
OHH...

755
00:30:20,718 --> 00:30:22,453
THEY LOOKED LIKE THEIR MOMS.

756
00:30:22,453 --> 00:30:24,022
THE BIG EYES,
YOU SEE THAT LITTLE LIPS.

757
00:30:24,022 --> 00:30:25,823
THERE'S NO TOP LIP THERE.

758
00:30:25,823 --> 00:30:28,126
THEY ACT AND TALK
LIKE THEIR MOMS.

759
00:30:28,126 --> 00:30:29,727
WHAT HAVE YOU BEEN DOING
TILL YOU CAME HERE?

760
00:30:31,562 --> 00:30:35,300
YOUR MOM WAS DANCING
WITH SIX BIKERS.

761
00:30:36,234 --> 00:30:38,870
BRITTANY'S MOM HAS A SENSE
OF HUMOR JUST LIKE BRITTANY.

762
00:30:38,870 --> 00:30:40,438
OH, YEAH.

763
00:30:40,438 --> 00:30:44,042
THEN YOU WIND HER UP
AND WIND HER UP TIGHT.

764
00:30:44,042 --> 00:30:47,645
DINNER'S READY!

765
00:30:47,645 --> 00:30:49,314
Tyra: HAVING BRITTANY
AND CHRISTINA'S MOMS AROUND

766
00:30:49,314 --> 00:30:52,717
MADE KAHLEN MISS HER FAMILY.

767
00:30:52,717 --> 00:30:55,386
BUT CALLS HOME
DIDN'T ALWAYS END HAPPILY.

768
00:30:55,386 --> 00:30:57,055
DAMMIT!

769
00:30:57,055 --> 00:30:58,956
I CHECKED MY MESSAGES

770
00:30:58,956 --> 00:31:00,892
AND ONE OF MY FRIENDS
FROM HIGH SCHOOL

771
00:31:00,892 --> 00:31:04,262
HAD, UM, HAD PASSED AWAY.

772
00:31:04,262 --> 00:31:05,830
I DON'T KNOW
IF I CAN HANDLE THIS.

773
00:31:05,830 --> 00:31:09,100
Tyra: IN A CHILLING COINCIDENCE,
THAT WEEK'S PHOTO SHOOT

774
00:31:09,100 --> 00:31:11,869
TOOK PLACE IN A CEMETERY.

775
00:31:11,869 --> 00:31:14,272
YOU GIRLS ARE GONNA HAVE
TO PORTRAY

776
00:31:14,272 --> 00:31:16,574
ONE OF THESE SEVEN DEADLY SINS

777
00:31:16,574 --> 00:31:18,743
AT THE BOTTOM
OF THIS EIGHT-FOOT GRAVE.

778
00:31:18,743 --> 00:31:21,212
Tyra: KAHLEN TRIED TO KEEP HER
EMOTIONS IN CHECK.

779
00:31:21,212 --> 00:31:23,614
BUT HAVING TO POSE
IN AN OPEN GRAVE

780
00:31:23,614 --> 00:31:25,383
PUSHED HER OVER THE EDGE.

781
00:31:25,383 --> 00:31:27,819
I JUST DON'T UNDERSTAND.

782
00:31:28,853 --> 00:31:32,423
(sobbing)

783
00:31:35,193 --> 00:31:38,196
Tyra: KAHLEN WAS ABLE TO USE
HER RAGE TO EMBODY

784
00:31:38,196 --> 00:31:41,232
THE DEADLY SIN OF WRATH
AND PUT IT IN HER PHOTOGRAPH.

785
00:31:41,232 --> 00:31:43,501
YEAH, THAT'S GREAT,
JUST KEEP IT RIGHT THERE.

786
00:31:43,501 --> 00:31:44,502
NICE.

787
00:31:44,502 --> 00:31:45,703
GIVE ME, GRR.

788
00:31:45,703 --> 00:31:47,205
(growling)

789
00:31:47,205 --> 00:31:48,573
OKAY, ONE MORE.

790
00:31:48,573 --> 00:31:50,341
(growling)

791
00:31:50,341 --> 00:31:52,143
Tyra: IN THE END,
KAHLEN PUSHED THROUGH HER GRIEF

792
00:31:52,143 --> 00:31:54,178
FOR A STUNNING PHOTOGRAPH.

793
00:31:54,178 --> 00:31:56,414
BUT TATIANA
COULDN'T MAKE THE GRADE.

794
00:31:56,414 --> 00:31:59,884
TATIANA ON A GLOBAL LEVEL,
EVEN FOR THE UNITED STATES,

795
00:31:59,884 --> 00:32:01,085
IS NOT TOP MODEL.

796
00:32:01,085 --> 00:32:03,421
SHE JUST ISN'T.

797
00:32:03,421 --> 00:32:05,256
Tyra: SO WE SENT HER HOME.

798
00:32:06,157 --> 00:32:08,826
Tatiana: I'M VERY DISAPPOINTED
IN MYSELF.

799
00:32:08,826 --> 00:32:10,628
BUT AT THE SAME TIME, I JUST--

800
00:32:10,628 --> 00:32:13,297
MAYBE IT WASN'T
THE RIGHT PATH FOR ME.

801
00:32:16,401 --> 00:32:18,770
Tyra: AND NOW
SOME MORE MODEL MOMENTS
FROM THE "TOP MODEL" VAULT.

802
00:32:18,770 --> 00:32:19,937
SO NOW, OF COURSE,
YOU GUYS KNOW,

803
00:32:19,937 --> 00:32:22,707
WE HAVE A CRAZY PANEL OF JUDGES
STARTING WITH...

804
00:32:22,707 --> 00:32:24,308
WHY AM I THE CRAZY?

805
00:32:24,308 --> 00:32:26,144
I DON'T KNOW WHY
YOU'RE CRAZY, JANICE.

806
00:32:26,144 --> 00:32:28,045
I'M GONNA COME OVER THERE
AND STRANGLE YOU.

807
00:32:28,045 --> 00:32:29,480
- ALL RIGHTY.
- CAN WE BOOT TWO TONIGHT?

808
00:32:29,480 --> 00:32:30,882
I LOVE YOU, JANICE.

809
00:32:30,882 --> 00:32:32,283
WELL, WAIT A MINUTE,
I'M ASKING--

810
00:32:32,283 --> 00:32:34,018
- OH, SHUT UP, JANICE.
- SHUT UP.

811
00:32:34,018 --> 00:32:35,353
SHUT UP, JANICE.

812
00:32:35,353 --> 00:32:37,522
- YOU BETTER THAN SHUT ME UP.
- THAT'S NOT POSSIBLE.

813
00:32:37,522 --> 00:32:41,959
THE LOVELY SANE...
JANICE DICKINSON.

814
00:32:41,959 --> 00:32:45,663
COMING UP NEXT, IT'S NIGHT
OF PASSION IN THE JUDGING ROOM.

815
00:32:45,663 --> 00:32:47,165
(screaming)

816
00:32:47,165 --> 00:32:49,400
AND IN THE HOUSE.

817
00:32:53,271 --> 00:32:55,506
Tyra: HIGH FASHION
HAPPENS ALL OVER THE WORLD.

818
00:32:55,506 --> 00:32:57,074
SO I HAD THE GIRLS
PACK THEIR BAGS

819
00:32:57,074 --> 00:32:59,544
TO HEAD FOR SOUTH AFRICA.

820
00:32:59,544 --> 00:33:01,212
GOODBYE, L.A.

821
00:33:01,212 --> 00:33:02,513
Tyra: THE GIRLS WERE EXCITED

822
00:33:02,513 --> 00:33:04,282
TO BEING THEIR SOUTH AFRICAN
ADVENTURE.

823
00:33:04,282 --> 00:33:06,117
- CHEERS.
- CHEERS.

824
00:33:06,117 --> 00:33:07,285
- TO AFRICA.
- TO AFRICA.

825
00:33:09,887 --> 00:33:12,190
Tyra: BUT MICHELLE FELT
AS ALONE ON THE PLANE

826
00:33:12,190 --> 00:33:15,193
AS SHE OFTEN FELT IN THE HOUSE.

827
00:33:15,193 --> 00:33:18,796
Michelle: I THINK THE GIRLS
PERCEIVE ME AS A LONER.

828
00:33:18,796 --> 00:33:21,299
AND I'VE BEEN TRYING
TO CONNECT WITH THEM MORE.

829
00:33:21,299 --> 00:33:25,670
ONCE AGAIN, EVERYONE'S LEAVING
ME HERE BY MYSELF.

830
00:33:25,670 --> 00:33:27,038
I THINK I HAVE A WAYS TO GO.

831
00:33:28,973 --> 00:33:33,077
(men singing)

832
00:33:34,378 --> 00:33:36,047
Tyra: WHEN THE GIRLS
GOT TO SOUTH AFRICA,

833
00:33:36,047 --> 00:33:38,549
A DETERMINED MICHELLE
TRIED TO RELATE.

834
00:33:38,549 --> 00:33:40,785
DID YOU READ THE PACKET?
IT SAID WHEN YOU'RE IN
A CONVERSATION,

835
00:33:40,785 --> 00:33:43,488
DON'T PUT YOUR HANDS IN YOUR
POCKET 'CAUSE THAT'S RUDE

836
00:33:43,488 --> 00:33:45,389
AND DON'T POINT
WITH YOUR INDEX FINGER.

837
00:33:45,389 --> 00:33:46,791
REALLY?

838
00:33:46,791 --> 00:33:48,960
WELL, THAT'S THE SAME RULE
AS IN AMERICA.

839
00:33:48,960 --> 00:33:50,862
YOU CAN'T DO THAT
IN AMERICA, EITHER.

840
00:33:53,531 --> 00:33:55,533
AFTER GOING ON SAFARI TONIGHT,

841
00:33:55,533 --> 00:33:58,135
THE GIRLS HAD SOME QUIET TIME
TO REFLECT.

842
00:33:58,135 --> 00:34:00,471
Michelle: I'VE LEARNED MORE
IN THIS PAST MONTH FROM YOU GUYS

843
00:34:00,471 --> 00:34:03,541
THAN I THINK I HAVE IN SCHOOL
OR, YOU KNOW, ANYTHING.

844
00:34:03,541 --> 00:34:04,675
'CAUSE THIS EXPERIENCE

845
00:34:04,675 --> 00:34:06,711
JUST KINDA THROWS EVERYTHING
AT YOU AT ONCE.

846
00:34:06,711 --> 00:34:09,547
OH, YEAH, SINCE, LIKE WHEN
WE VERY FIRST STARTED THIS,

847
00:34:09,547 --> 00:34:13,951
I WAS... A LITTLE MORE TIMID,
SHY, SORT OF.

848
00:34:13,951 --> 00:34:17,388
THIS EXPERIENCE KIND OF LIKE
MAKES YOU CONFRONT WHO YOU ARE.

849
00:34:17,388 --> 00:34:18,689
OH, YEAH.

850
00:34:18,689 --> 00:34:20,358
NOT THE PERSON THAT YOU PRETEND
TO BE ON THE OUTSIDE.

851
00:34:20,358 --> 00:34:22,693
IT MAKES YOU DEAL WITH
THE PERSON THAT YOU ARE INSIDE.

852
00:34:22,693 --> 00:34:24,227
Kahlen: I THINK MICHELLE'S
MADE THE MOST PROGRESS

853
00:34:24,227 --> 00:34:25,428
OUT OF ANY OF US.

854
00:34:25,428 --> 00:34:27,598
YOU KNOW, PICTURE AFTER PICTURE,
YOU'RE AMAZED.

855
00:34:27,598 --> 00:34:29,000
YOU'RE LIKE,
MICHELLE, IS THAT YOU?

856
00:34:29,000 --> 00:34:32,270
THE ONLY THING THAT MICHELLE
NEEDS NOW IS TO LEARN

857
00:34:32,270 --> 00:34:34,604
HOW TO JUST RELAX
AND LET SOME OF THOSE NERVES OUT

858
00:34:34,604 --> 00:34:37,408
AND SOME OF THE TENSION OUT.

859
00:34:37,408 --> 00:34:39,310
Tyra: KEENYAH HAD CONCERNS
OF HER OWN.

860
00:34:39,310 --> 00:34:40,477
LIKE HER RECENT WEIGHT GAIN.

861
00:34:44,048 --> 00:34:46,350
KEENYAH CAN SNACK LIKE NO OTHER.

862
00:34:46,817 --> 00:34:49,153
SHE HAS GAINED
ABOUT TEN POUNDS.

863
00:34:49,153 --> 00:34:50,988
SO YOU THINK TOMORROW,
IF I DON'T EAT--

864
00:34:50,988 --> 00:34:53,357
NO, DON'T EVER NOT EAT.

865
00:34:53,357 --> 00:34:54,492
BECAUSE YOU'VE BEEN
GAINING WEIGHT,

866
00:34:54,492 --> 00:34:55,626
YOU JUST HAVEN'T
BEEN WATCHING WHAT YOU EAT.

867
00:34:55,626 --> 00:34:57,495
JUNK FOOD, WHICH HAS TONS
OF SODIUM,

868
00:34:57,495 --> 00:34:59,062
YOU'RE RETAINING TONS OF WATER.

869
00:34:59,062 --> 00:35:01,098
Tyra: AT THE PHOTO SHOOT
LATER THAT DAY,

870
00:35:01,098 --> 00:35:03,301
KEENYAH HAD TO PORTRAY
AN ELEPHANT

871
00:35:03,301 --> 00:35:05,069
WITH A REVEALING COSTUME.

872
00:35:05,069 --> 00:35:08,306
Keenyah: THE STOMACH IS EXPOSED,
IT'S BLOATED.

873
00:35:08,306 --> 00:35:10,708
I HAVE TO JUST TRY
TO SUCK IT IN AND WORK IT.

874
00:35:10,708 --> 00:35:12,376
Tyra: FOR THE JUDGING CHALLENGE,

875
00:35:12,376 --> 00:35:14,278
THE GIRLS HAD TO POSE
WITH AN OBJECT

876
00:35:14,278 --> 00:35:15,780
WHILE DISPLAYING AN EMOTION.

877
00:35:15,780 --> 00:35:17,915
NAIMA ALMOST NAILED IT.

878
00:35:17,915 --> 00:35:19,383
MICHELLE LOOKED NERVOUS.

879
00:35:19,383 --> 00:35:21,586
MICHELLE, YOU LOOKED
QUITE SCARED THE WHOLE TIME.

880
00:35:21,586 --> 00:35:23,654
KAHLEN AND CHRISTINA
LACKED PASSION.

881
00:35:23,654 --> 00:35:25,890
SO JANICE DECIDED TO SHOW THEM
HOW IT'S DONE.

882
00:35:25,890 --> 00:35:29,260
(screaming/laughing)

883
00:35:30,428 --> 00:35:33,297
- WAIT, WAIT!
- JANICE!

884
00:35:33,297 --> 00:35:34,966
PERHAPS I CAN GET INVOLVED.

885
00:35:36,334 --> 00:35:39,036
THAT'S JUST GIRLS HAVING FUN.

886
00:35:39,036 --> 00:35:40,671
THAT'S PASSION.

887
00:35:40,671 --> 00:35:44,008
DURING EVALUATIONS, KEENYAH'S
PICTURE WAS A BIG PROBLEM.

888
00:35:44,008 --> 00:35:47,111
THIS PHOTO IS REALLY BEAUTIFUL,
KEENYAH, BUT I HATE TO SAY IT,

889
00:35:47,111 --> 00:35:50,281
THEY HAD TO DO A LOT OF BODY
WORK ON YOU IN RE-TOUCHING.

890
00:35:50,281 --> 00:35:51,716
I THINK IT'S
ALL ABOUT CHOICES, KEENYAH.

891
00:35:51,716 --> 00:35:53,317
YOU CAN GET A BURGER
AND TAKE THE BREAD OFF.

892
00:35:53,484 --> 00:35:57,521
BUT IN THE END, THIS COMPETITION
PROVED TOO MUCH FOR MICHELLE.

893
00:35:57,521 --> 00:35:59,390
MICHELLE,
BEING A TOP MODEL MEANS

894
00:35:59,390 --> 00:36:01,459
BEING UNDER PRESSURE CONSTANTLY.

895
00:36:01,459 --> 00:36:03,527
WE'RE NOT SURE IF YOU'RE
STRONG ENOUGH FOR THAT.

896
00:36:03,527 --> 00:36:08,232
SO WE HAD TO SEND HER HOME.

897
00:36:12,370 --> 00:36:15,272
BACK AT THE HOTEL,
NAIMA AND CHRISTINA PLOTTED

898
00:36:15,272 --> 00:36:18,009
TO PUT A LITTLE PASSION
INTO KAHLEN'S CONFESSIONAL.

899
00:36:18,009 --> 00:36:21,245
I'M BECOMING MORE COMFORTABLE...

900
00:36:21,245 --> 00:36:23,114
WITH MY OWN, YOU KNOW,
UNDER MY SKIN.

901
00:36:26,083 --> 00:36:27,818
I AM STILL NAIVE TO THIS WORLD.

902
00:36:27,818 --> 00:36:30,821
I'M STILL ON THE ROAD
TO FINDING OUT WHO I TRULY AM.

903
00:36:30,821 --> 00:36:32,590
- (door opens)
- KAHLEN!

904
00:36:32,590 --> 00:36:33,824
DO YOU WANNA SEE PASSION?

905
00:36:33,824 --> 00:36:35,459
- I WANT PASSION.
- COME ON, SHOW HER PASSION.

906
00:36:37,728 --> 00:36:41,666
(shrieking)

907
00:36:41,666 --> 00:36:45,036
TELL YOUR LOVE
I'M GOING TO SEE YOU.

908
00:36:45,036 --> 00:36:47,004
(Naima screaming)

909
00:36:47,004 --> 00:36:48,606
(laughing)

910
00:36:49,440 --> 00:36:52,643
YOU WANT ME TO TAKE THAT,
YOU WANT ME TO TALK THAT?

911
00:36:52,643 --> 00:36:54,712
- GOT IT.
- THERE YOU GO, PASSION!

912
00:36:54,712 --> 00:36:56,414
(laughing)

913
00:36:56,414 --> 00:36:58,115
I FELT TONGUE AROUND THAT GRAPE.

914
00:36:58,115 --> 00:36:59,150
YUP.

915
00:36:59,150 --> 00:37:00,284
(laughing)

916
00:37:00,284 --> 00:37:02,953
SOMETIMES CHRISTINA
IS VERY SERIOUS.

917
00:37:02,953 --> 00:37:05,423
LIKE, SOMETIMES I REALLY SEE
CHRISTINA JUST--

918
00:37:05,423 --> 00:37:08,693
HAVE FUN AND JUST LIKE
JOKE AROUND AND PLAY.

919
00:37:08,693 --> 00:37:13,631
IT'S DIFFICULT FOR HER TO BRING
THAT PERSON WITH HER TO PANEL.

920
00:37:14,699 --> 00:37:16,367
Tyra: WHEN I DROPPED BY
FOR DINNER,

921
00:37:16,367 --> 00:37:19,003
CHRISTINA'S COLDNESS
WAS THE TOPIC OF DISCUSSION.

922
00:37:19,003 --> 00:37:20,371
LIKE WHEN I'M WITH THESE GIRLS,
LIKE,

923
00:37:20,371 --> 00:37:23,074
I'M SO HAPPY AND SO WARM
AND SO FUNNY AND STUFF.

924
00:37:23,074 --> 00:37:25,309
BUT WHEN I GET IN THAT ROOM,
I FEEL LIKE, FOR SOME REASON,

925
00:37:25,309 --> 00:37:27,078
I HOLD BACK
WHEN IT COMES TO PANEL.

926
00:37:27,078 --> 00:37:29,146
AND I DON'T KNOW IF IT'S NERVES,
INTIMIDATION, WHAT IT IS,

927
00:37:29,146 --> 00:37:31,716
BUT IT'S LIKE, I SEE MYSELF
AS A TOTALLY DIFFERENT PERSON

928
00:37:31,716 --> 00:37:33,184
EVERY TIME I'M IN THAT ROOM.

929
00:37:33,184 --> 00:37:35,086
YOU HAVE TO JUST PRETEND WE'RE
SITTING THERE IN OUR UNDERWEAR.

930
00:37:35,086 --> 00:37:37,655
YOU IN YOUR UNDERWEAR
IS GONNA BE BEAUTIFUL

931
00:37:37,655 --> 00:37:40,458
SO THAT'S NOT GONNA HELP.

932
00:37:40,458 --> 00:37:42,760
Tyra: THE NEXT DAY,
THE GIRLS WENT ON GO-SEES

933
00:37:42,760 --> 00:37:43,928
WITH THE TOP PEOPLE

934
00:37:43,928 --> 00:37:45,730
IN THE SOUTH AFRICAN
FASHION INDUSTRY.

935
00:37:45,730 --> 00:37:47,098
Christina: I'M A LITTLE NERVOUS
TO GO IN THERE

936
00:37:47,098 --> 00:37:48,265
AND HAVE TO SELL YOURSELF

937
00:37:48,265 --> 00:37:49,533
BECAUSE THAT'S ONE THING,
I'M HONESTLY,

938
00:37:49,533 --> 00:37:50,835
NOT REALLY GOOD AT.

939
00:37:50,835 --> 00:37:54,538
Tyra: ONCE AGAIN, CHRISTINA
HAD TROUBLE WARMING UP.

940
00:37:54,538 --> 00:37:57,775
(cricket chirping)

941
00:37:57,775 --> 00:37:59,677
KAHLEN HAD TROUBLE BEING EDGY.

942
00:37:59,677 --> 00:38:02,313
IF YOU LOOK AT YOUR PICTURES,
IT LOOKS VERY INNOCENT.

943
00:38:02,313 --> 00:38:03,881
I THINK AT THE MOMENT,
IN SOUTH AFRICA,

944
00:38:03,881 --> 00:38:06,650
WE DEFINITELY
GOT MORE EDGE TO IT.

945
00:38:06,650 --> 00:38:10,020
Tyra: BUT KEENYAH HAD NO TROUBLE
AT ALL BEING COMPETITIVE.

946
00:38:10,020 --> 00:38:11,989
Keenyah: NAIMA WAS THERE FIRST,
I CAME SECOND.

947
00:38:11,989 --> 00:38:13,991
MAYBE I SHOULD JUST WAIT
BUT IT'S A COMPETITION.

948
00:38:13,991 --> 00:38:15,793
HI, I'M KEENYAH.

949
00:38:15,793 --> 00:38:17,862
Tyra: LITERALLY PUSHING
HER COMPETITORS OUT OF THE WAY.

950
00:38:17,862 --> 00:38:20,965
KEENYAH'S VERY COMPETITIVE,
THAT'S JUST HOW SHE IS.

951
00:38:20,965 --> 00:38:23,234
AND I THINK SHE FEELS THAT
SHE HAS TO STEP IT UP EVEN MORE

952
00:38:23,234 --> 00:38:24,935
TO MAKE UP FOR HER WEIGHT.

953
00:38:26,403 --> 00:38:28,806
Tyra: AT THE PHOTO SHOOT,
KAHLEN STILL STRUGGLED.

954
00:38:28,806 --> 00:38:31,175
DO YOU FEEL SEXY TODAY?

955
00:38:31,175 --> 00:38:32,877
I DON'T BELIEVE YOU.

956
00:38:32,877 --> 00:38:35,946
Tyra: AND KEENYAH WAS QUICK
TO POINT OUT KAHLEN'S FAULTS.

957
00:38:35,946 --> 00:38:37,882
Keenyah: ONE THING THAT I GUESS
YOU WERE CHALLENGED WITH TODAY

958
00:38:37,882 --> 00:38:40,251
WHICH WAS YOUR INNOCENCE AGAIN.

959
00:38:40,251 --> 00:38:42,987
REMEMBER OUR GO-SEE THINGS,
THEY SAID, LOTS OF INNOCENCE.

960
00:38:42,987 --> 00:38:44,221
INNOCENCE, INNOCENCE.

961
00:38:44,221 --> 00:38:45,656
Kahlen: YEAH, THAT WAS
JUST ONE GIRL, THOUGH.

962
00:38:45,656 --> 00:38:48,893
WITH KEENYAH, I FEEL LIKE SHE
HAS TO CUT OTHER PEOPLE DOWN

963
00:38:48,893 --> 00:38:51,228
TO MAKE HERSELF FEEL BETTER
ABOUT HERSELF.

964
00:38:51,228 --> 00:38:53,597
AS THE WEEKS GO ON, I JUST--
I CAN'T TAKE IT.

965
00:38:53,597 --> 00:38:56,000
Tyra: AND ALTHOUGH,
CHRISTINA BARED HER BODY,

966
00:38:56,000 --> 00:38:58,769
SHE HAD A HARD TIME
BARING HER SOUL.

967
00:38:58,769 --> 00:39:01,839
IF YOU WALKED IN MY DOORS,
I DON'T KNOW HOW I'D SELL YOU

968
00:39:01,839 --> 00:39:03,808
BECAUSE I'M NOT FEELING
ANYTHING FROM YOU.

969
00:39:03,808 --> 00:39:06,911
I DON'T KNOW WHERE
CONFIDENCE MEETS COLD.

970
00:39:06,911 --> 00:39:10,548
WHAT WE WANNA SEE IS FIRE
COMING FROM WITHIN,

971
00:39:10,548 --> 00:39:12,416
AND YOU'RE NOT
GETTING IT AT ALL.

972
00:39:12,416 --> 00:39:14,685
Tyra: SO SHE WAS SENT HOME.

973
00:39:14,685 --> 00:39:19,423
I KNOW I'M NOT THIS COLD...
LIKE, RESERVED PERSON.

974
00:39:19,423 --> 00:39:22,526
I JUST DON'T KNOW-- I DON'T
UNDERSTAND WHAT HAPPENED TO ME.

975
00:39:27,131 --> 00:39:28,432
Tyra: BEING IN SOUTH AFRICA

976
00:39:28,432 --> 00:39:30,701
MADE KEENYAH PROUD TO GET
IN TOUCH WITH HER ROOTS.

977
00:39:30,701 --> 00:39:33,404
IT'S GOOD TO COME HERE,
NOT THAT IT'S MORE IMPORTANT

978
00:39:33,404 --> 00:39:35,039
TO ME THAN THEM
'CAUSE THEY'RE NOT BLACK.

979
00:39:35,039 --> 00:39:36,307
I'M BLACK.

980
00:39:36,307 --> 00:39:38,042
I'M BLACK AND I DO FEEL LIKE
THIS IS MY HOME.

981
00:39:38,042 --> 00:39:39,743
THIS IS WHERE MY ROOTS ARE.

982
00:39:39,743 --> 00:39:42,546
TO ME, BEING BLACK,
I WAS LIKE, THAT'S SOMETHING

983
00:39:42,546 --> 00:39:45,616
THAT I HAVE TO DO BEFORE I DIE,
I HAVE TO GO TO AFRICA.

984
00:39:45,616 --> 00:39:47,918
I'VE HEARD HER SAY IT
SO MANY TIMES, THIS JUST MEANS

985
00:39:47,918 --> 00:39:49,353
SO MUCH TO ME 'CAUSE I'M BLACK
AND IT'S JUST LIKE,

986
00:39:49,353 --> 00:39:51,088
OKAY, ALL RIGHT, GREAT.

987
00:39:51,088 --> 00:39:54,625
I KNOW THIS EXPERIENCE MEANS
A LOT TO NAIMA AS WELL.

988
00:39:54,625 --> 00:39:57,228
Tyra: THE TENSION GREW ON A TRIP

989
00:39:57,228 --> 00:39:59,563
TO NELSON MANDELA'S
FORMER PRISON CELL.

990
00:39:59,563 --> 00:40:00,698
ONE OF YOU LADIES WILL HAVE

991
00:40:00,698 --> 00:40:03,467
THE PLEASURE TO OPEN
MR. MANDELA'S CELL.

992
00:40:03,467 --> 00:40:05,836
KEENYAH WANTED TO UNLOCK IT.

993
00:40:05,836 --> 00:40:09,506
SHE THINKS JUST BECAUSE
SHE'S THE BLACK ONE

994
00:40:09,506 --> 00:40:11,242
THAT SHE DESERVES TO OPEN IT.

995
00:40:11,242 --> 00:40:13,477
I DON'T REALLY THINK
OF NAIMA AS BLACK.

996
00:40:13,477 --> 00:40:15,346
I JUST DON'T SEE THAT IN HER.

997
00:40:15,346 --> 00:40:19,750
MY FATHER IS BLACK
AND MEXICO-INDIAN.

998
00:40:19,750 --> 00:40:21,986
MY MAMA IS BLACK AND IRISH.

999
00:40:21,986 --> 00:40:24,555
I'M NOT THE TYPICAL BLACK GIRL

1000
00:40:24,555 --> 00:40:26,891
BUT IT MEANS A LOT
FOR ME BEING HERE.

1001
00:40:26,891 --> 00:40:30,361
1964 TO 1982.

1002
00:40:30,361 --> 00:40:33,797
THAT'S THE COURAGE
OF THAT ONE MAN KEPT US GOING.

1003
00:40:33,797 --> 00:40:36,533
I DIDN'T EVEN THINK THAT KEENYAH
KNEW WHO HE WAS.

1004
00:40:36,533 --> 00:40:39,003
SHE DOESN'T KNOW
IF HE'S ALIVE OR NOT.

1005
00:40:39,003 --> 00:40:41,438
SO I DIDN'T UNDERSTAND WHY
SHE WAS GETTING SO EMOTIONAL.

1006
00:40:43,374 --> 00:40:45,943
Tyra: AND LATER
THE TENSION EXPLODED.

1007
00:40:45,943 --> 00:40:48,045
WHEN HE GAVE HER THE KEY,
YOU CRIED ABOUT IT.

1008
00:40:48,045 --> 00:40:51,482
YOU DIDN'T EVEN KNOW
IF HE WAS STILL ALIVE OR NOT.

1009
00:40:51,482 --> 00:40:52,616
IT WAS AN EMOTIONAL
MOMENT FOR ME.

1010
00:40:52,616 --> 00:40:53,784
YOU WERE NOT IN MY SHOES,

1011
00:40:53,784 --> 00:40:55,786
YOU DON'T KNOW
HOW I FELT AT THAT MOMENT.

1012
00:40:55,786 --> 00:40:58,222
YOU ARE JUST SAYING THIS
'CAUSE YOU'RE BLACK,

1013
00:40:58,222 --> 00:40:59,323
YOU'VE SAID IT A MILLION TIMES.

1014
00:40:59,323 --> 00:41:01,091
WHAT YOU THINK?
YEAH, 'CAUSE I'M BLACK!

1015
00:41:01,091 --> 00:41:05,362
OH MY GOD!
SHUT UP!

1016
00:41:07,965 --> 00:41:09,667
Tyra: THE FIGHTING TOOK
ITS TOLL ON BRITTANY

1017
00:41:09,667 --> 00:41:12,002
AND SHE WASN'T HERSELF
DURING JUDGING.

1018
00:41:12,002 --> 00:41:13,170
PERSONALITY'S JUST NOT THERE.

1019
00:41:13,170 --> 00:41:14,471
WHERE'S MY BRITTANY.

1020
00:41:14,471 --> 00:41:16,507
MY GIRL NEED TO REALLY SPICE IT
UP A LITTLE BIT MORE.

1021
00:41:16,507 --> 00:41:18,742
Tyra: SO WE DECIDED
TO SEND HER HOME.

1022
00:41:18,742 --> 00:41:20,277
THANK YOU SO MUCH.

1023
00:41:20,277 --> 00:41:23,580
IT'S JUST HARD
WHEN YOU'RE SO CLOSE AND YET...

1024
00:41:23,580 --> 00:41:25,883
...SO FAR.

1025
00:41:33,324 --> 00:41:35,659
Tyra: NOW IT'S DOWN
TO THE FINAL THREE.

1026
00:41:35,659 --> 00:41:38,295
KEENYAH, THE SUPER CONFIDENT
COMPTON BEAUTY

1027
00:41:38,295 --> 00:41:39,663
WITH A COMPETITIVE EDGE.

1028
00:41:39,663 --> 00:41:42,299
NAIMA, THE MOHAWK DANCER
FROM DETROIT

1029
00:41:42,299 --> 00:41:44,368
STRUGGLING TO MAKE
HER PERSONALITY POP.

1030
00:41:44,368 --> 00:41:46,503
AND KAHLEN,
THE SHY OKLAHOMA GIRL

1031
00:41:46,503 --> 00:41:48,305
STRIVING TO SHED HER INSECURITY.

1032
00:41:48,305 --> 00:41:50,140
WHO WILL BE
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL"?

1033
00:41:50,140 --> 00:41:52,543
TUNE IN TOMORROW NIGHT
TO FIND OUT.

1034
00:41:55,846 --> 00:41:59,183
♪ NAH-NAH-NAH-NAH-NAH ♪♪

1035
